{'symbol': 'MMM', 'date': '2019-10-24 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': '3M Sees 2019 Organic Growth In China Down Mid-Single Digits - Conf Call', 'text': "3M CO EXPECTS ORGANIC GROWTH IN CHINA TO BE DOWN MID-SINGLE DIGITS IN 2019 - CONF CALL.3M CO SAYS WHILE SELLING PRICES WERE LOWER THAN EXPECTED IN Q3, CO’S SOURCING EFFORTS REDUCED RAW MATERIAL COST RESULTING IN A NET BENEFIT, WHICH IS EXPECT TO CONTINUE GOING FORWARD.3M CO SAYS RAISING EXPECTATIONS FOR 2019 FREE CASH FLOW CONVERSION TO A RANGE OF 105% TO 110% VERSUS 95% TO 105% PREVIOUSLY.3M CO SAYS CAPITAL EXPENDITURES REMAIN ON TRACK TO BE IN THE RANGE OF $1.6 BILLION TO $1.7 BILLION FOR THE YEAR.3M CO SAYS ANTICIPATE Q4 EPS IN THE RANGE OF $2.05 TO $2.15 AND AN ORGANIC SALES DECLINE OF 1% TO 3%.3M CO SAYS CO TESTIFIED BEFORE A CONGRESSIONAL SUBCOMMITTEE IN WASHINGTON IN SEPT. AND REMINDED THE COMMITTEE THAT SCIENTIFIC EVIDENCE DOES NOT SHOW PFAS CAUSING ADVERSE HUMAN HEALTH EFFECTS AT CURRENT OR HISTORICAL LEVELS.3M'S POSITION ON PFAS IS SHARED BY PUBLIC HEALTH AGENCIES AND INDEPENDENT SCIENCE REVIEW PANELS.3M SAYS CHANNEL RESPONSE TO DECLINE IN DEMAND IN AUTOMOTIVE AND ELECTRONICS MORE BROADLY TOOK PLACE IN H1 2019, BUT 3M SAW ADDITIONAL ADJUSTMENTS, A BIG PART OF THAT IN CHINA IN Q3.3M SAYS, ABSENT A RECESSION AND SOME OTHER MAJOR DOWNTURN IN THE MARKETS IN 2020, CO EXPECTS TO HAVE POSITIVE GROWTH ACROSS BUSINESSES.WITH RESPECT TO FOUR END MARKETS IN ELECTRONICS, 3M SAYS CONSUMER ELECTRONICS SAW SOFTNESS CONTINUE TO COME THROUGH IN Q3."}{'symbol': 'MMM', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': '3M Sees FY 2019 GAAP Earnings Per Share $8.20 To $8.30', 'text': '3M REPORTS THIRD-QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.72.Q3 SALES $8.0 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $8.16 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.49 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $8.99 TO $9.09 EXCLUDING ITEMS.SEES FY 2019 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $8.20 TO $8.30.SEES Q4 2019 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.05 TO $2.15.QTRLY ORGANIC LOCAL-CURRENCY SALES DECLINED 1.3 PERCENT YEAR-ON-YEAR.MACROECONOMIC ENVIRONMENT REMAINS CHALLENGING.CONTINUED TO EFFECTIVELY MANAGE COSTS AND REDUCE INVENTORY LEVELS.WHILE MACROECONOMIC ENVIRONMENT REMAINS CHALLENGING, WE EXECUTED WELL AND BUILT ON PROGRESS WE MADE IN Q2.FOREIGN CURRENCY TRANSLATION REDUCED SALES BY 1.3 PERCENT YEAR-ON-YEAR IN QUARTER.3M UPDATED ITS FULL-YEAR 2019 GAAP EARNINGS TO BE IN RANGE OF $8.20 TO $8.30 PER SHARE.3M ALSO UPDATED ITS FULL-YEAR ORGANIC LOCAL-CURRENCY SALES GUIDANCE TO DECLINE BETWEEN 1% TO 1.5%.QTRLY NET SALES FOR SAFETY AND INDUSTRIAL   SEGMENT OF $2,849 MILLION VERSUS $3,021 MILLION.FOURTH-QUARTER 2019 GAAP EARNINGS GUIDANCE INCLUDES AN ESTIMATED $0.15 PER SHARE NEGATIVE IMPACT FROM RECENTLY CLOSED ACQUISITION OF ACELITY.FOURTH-QUARTER ORGANIC LOCAL-CURRENCY SALES IS EXPECTED TO DECLINE BETWEEN 1 TO 3 PERCENT.EXCLUDING FULL-YEAR 2019 IMPACTS CO NOW EXPECTS ITS 2019 EARNINGS TO BE IN RANGE OF $8.99 TO $9.09 PER SHARE.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $9.29 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.41 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'MMM', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': '3M Company Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter and Full Year of 2019', 'text': '3M Company provided earnings guidance for the fourth quarter and full year of 2019. The company provided its fourth-quarter 2019 GAAP earnings guidance to be in the range of $2.05 to $2.15 per share. This earnings range includes an estimated $0.15 per share negative impact from the recently closed acquisition of Acelity Inc., which was previously not included in guidance. The company updated its full-year 2019 GAAP earnings to be in the range of $8.20 to $8.30 per share versus a prior expectation of $8.25 to $8.75 per share. Excluding the full-year 2019 impacts from the first-quarter significant litigation-related charges of $0.72 per share, the second-quarter deconsolidation of its Venezuelan subsidiary charge of $0.28 per share, and the gas and flame detection divestiture gain of $0.21 per share, 3M now expects its 2019 earnings to be in the range of $8.99 to $9.09 per share versus prior expectation of $9.25 to $9.75. This updated earnings range includes an estimated $0.15 per share negative impact from the recently closed acquisition of Acelity Inc., which was previously not included in full-year guidance.'}{'symbol': 'ABBV', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Abbvie Inc. Announces Collaboration with Cystic Fibrosis Foundation with', 'text': 'AbbVie and the Cystic Fibrosis Foundation announced a strategic collaboration in which AbbVie will develop a cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator (CFTR) potentiator compound licensed from the Foundation. Under the terms of the agreement, AbbVie will advance the potentiator into clinical development for potential use in combination treatments for cystic fibrosis. Cystic fibrosis is a life-threatening, progressive, genetic disease that causes persistent lung infections and limits the ability to breathe over time. In people with CF, mutations in the CFTR gene cause the CFTR protein to become dysfunctional.'}{'symbol': 'AFL', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Aflac Incorporated Declares Cash Dividend for the Fourth Quarter of Year 2019, Payable on December 02, 2019', 'text': 'Aflac Incorporated declared cash dividend of $0.27 per share for the fourth quarter of 2019. The payment date is December 02, 2019 to shareholders of record at the close of business on November 20, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'ALK', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Alaska Air Group, Inc. Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Alaska Air Group, Inc. announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced total revenue was USD 2,389 million compared to USD 2,212 million a year ago. Net income was USD 322 million compared to USD 217 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 2.61 compared to USD 1.76 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 2.6 compared to USD 1.75 a year ago. For the nine months, total revenue was USD 6,553 million compared to USD 6,200 million a year ago. Net income was USD 588 million compared to USD 414 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 4.76 compared to USD 3.36 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 4.74 compared to USD 3.34 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'ALB', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Albemarle Corporation Provides Earnings Guidance for the Third Quarter of 2019; Revises Financial Guidance for the Full Year 2019', 'text': 'Albemarle Corporation provided earnings guidance for the third quarter of 2019. The company expects third quarter 2019 diluted earnings per share to be approximately $1.46 on net income of approximately $155 million. The company revised financial guidance for the full year 2019. The company now expects net sales to be in the range of $3.6 billion to $3.7 billion against $3.65 billion to $3.85 billion as previously forecasted.'}{'symbol': 'ALXN', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Alexion Pharmaceuticals Q3 Non-GAAP Earnings Per Share $2.79', 'text': 'ALEXION REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.79.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.08.Q3 REVENUE $1.263 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.24 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.47 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ALEXION PHARMACEUTICALS - NEGATIVE IMPACT OF FOREIGN CURRENCY ON QTRLY TOTAL REVENUE YEAR-OVER-YEAR WAS LESS THAN 1%, OR $2.5 MILLION.INCREASING 2019 REVENUES AND EPS GUIDANCE.SEES 2019 TOTAL REVENUES $4,860 MILLION TO $4,890 MILLION.SEES  2019 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $8.58 TO $8.78.SEES 2019 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $10.25 TO $10.40.ALEXION PHARMACEUTICALS - UPDATED 2019 GUIDANCE ASSUMES GAAP EFFECTIVE TAX RATE OF 5% TO 6% & NON-GAAP EFFECTIVE TAX RATE OF 13% TO 14% FOR YEAR.UPDATED GUIDANCE EXCLUDES FINANCIAL IMPACT OF AGREEMENT TO ACQUIRE ACHILLION.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $9.94, REVENUE VIEW $4.85 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'ALGN', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Align Technology Posts Q3 EPS Of $1.28', 'text': 'ALIGN TECHNOLOGY ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q3 REVENUES UP 20.2% YEAR-OVER-YEAR TO A RECORD $607.3 MILLION.Q3 NET PROFIT OF $102.5 MILLION AND $1.28 DILUTED EPS.SEES Q4 2019 REVENUE $640 MILLION TO $650 MILLION.SEES Q4 DILUTED EPS IN RANGE OF $1.35 TO $1.42.EXPECT TO REPURCHASE AT LEAST $100 MILLION OF OUR STOCK IN OPEN MARKET IN Q4.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.14, REVENUE VIEW $594.0 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.35, REVENUE VIEW $639.3 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'ALLE', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Allegion plc Provides Earnings Guidance for the Full Year 2019', 'text': 'Allegion plc provided earnings guidance for the full year 2019. The company is affirming its full-year 2019 revenue outlook for total and organic growth to a range of 4.5% to 5.5% compared to 2018. The company is tightening its full-year 2019 outlook for reported EPS to a range of $4.55 to $4.65.'}{'symbol': 'LNT', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Alliant Energy Corporation, Q3 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 07, 2019', 'text': 'Alliant Energy Corporation, Q3 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 07, 2019'}{'symbol': 'GOOGL', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Verily Announces Partnerships With VAPAHCS & Atrius Health', 'text': 'Oct 24  - Alphabet Inc <GOOGL.O>::VERILY - ANNOUNCED PARTNERSHIPS WITH VAPAHCS AND ATRIUS HEALTH TO EVALUATE AND DEPLOY NEW TOOLS AND INTERVENTIONS AIMED AT OPTIMIZING CARE DELIVERY.'}{'symbol': 'AMZN', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Amazon.Com, Inc. Announces Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter 2019', 'text': 'Amazon.com, Inc. announced earnings guidance for the fourth quarter 2019. For the quarter, Net sales are expected to be between $80.0 billion and $86.5 billion, or to grow between 11% and 20% compared with fourth quarter 2018. Operating income is expected to be between $1.2 billion and $2.9 billion, compared with $3.8 billion in fourth quarter 2018.'}{'symbol': 'AAL', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'American Airlines Group Inc Says Expects To Pay $4.3 Billion In Capex In 2019', 'text': 'AMERICAN AIRLINES GROUP INC - EXPECTS TO PAY $4.3 BILLION IN CAPEX IN 2019, INCLUDING $2.6 BILLION IN AIRCRAFT AND $1.7 BILLION IN NON-AIRCRAFT CAPEX.AMERICAN AIRLINES - IN 2020, SEES TOTAL CAPEX TO DECLINE BY ABOUT $600 MILLION WITH AIRCRAFT CAPEX SPEND OF $2.0 BILLION, NON-AIRCRAFT CAPEX SPEND OF $1.7 BILLION.AMERICAN AIRLINES - FOR 2021, SEES CAPEX FALLING BY $1.5 BILLION WITH AIRCRAFT CAPEX SPEND EXPECTED TO BE $0.9 BILLION & NON-AIRCRAFT CAPEX EXPECTED TO BE $1.2 BILLION.AMERICAN AIRLINES GROUP INC - UPDATED DELIVERY SCHEDULE FOR THE REMAINDER OF 2019 BY MOVING 11 BOEING 737 MAX AIRCRAFT FROM 2019 INTO 2020.'}{'symbol': 'AAL', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'American Airlines Group Inc. Declares Dividend, Payable on Nov. 20, 2019', 'text': 'American Airlines Group Inc. declared dividend of 10 cents per share to be paid on Nov. 20 to stockholders of record as of Nov. 6, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'AEP', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Aep Reports Q3 Earnings, Raises And Narrows Full-Year Earnings Guidance Range', 'text': 'AEP REPORTS STRONG THIRD-QUARTER 2019 EARNINGS, RAISES AND NARROWS FULL-YEAR EARNINGS GUIDANCE RANGE.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.49.Q3 OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.46.SEES FY 2019 NON-GAAP OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.14 TO $4.24.RAISES AND NARROWS FULL-YEAR OPERATING EARNINGS (NON-GAAP) GUIDANCE RANGE TO $4.14 TO $4.24 PER SHARE.QTRLY REVENUE $4.3 BILLION VERSUS $4.3 BILLION.SEES FY 2019 ESTIMATED EPS ON A GAAP BASIS $4.07 TO $4.17.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.32, REVENUE VIEW $4.71 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $4.15, REVENUE VIEW $16.41 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'AEP', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'American Electric Power Company, Inc. Provides Earnings Guidance for the Year 2019', 'text': 'American Electric Power Company, Inc. provided earnings guidance for the year 2019. AEP management increased and narrowed its 2019 operating earnings guidance range to $4.14 to $4.24 per share from $4.00 to $4.20 per share.'}{'symbol': 'AXP', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'American Express Company Presents at Bank of America Merrill Lynch Future of Financials Conference, Nov-05-2019 11:20 AM', 'text': 'American Express Company Presents at Bank of America Merrill Lynch Future of Financials Conference, Nov-05-2019 11:20 AM. Venue: The St. Regis Hotel, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Douglas E. Buckminster, Group President of Global Consumer Services.'}{'symbol': 'AMP', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ameriprise Financial Reports Q3 Adjusted Operating Earnings Per Share Of $4.12', 'text': 'AMERIPRISE FINANCIAL REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.12.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $4.10 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.AMERIPRISE FINANCIAL - ASSETS UNDER MANAGEMENT & ADMINISTRATION WERE $921 BILLION, WITH ADVICE & WEALTH MANAGEMENT TOTAL CLIENT ASSETS OF $612 BILLION IN QUARTER.'}{'symbol': 'ANSS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ANSYS, Inc. (NasdaqGS:ANSS) entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Dynardo GmbH.', 'text': "ANSYS, Inc. (NasdaqGS:ANSS) entered into a definitive agreement to acquire Dynardo GmbH on October 24, 2019. The transaction is expected to close in the fourth quarter of 2019. The transaction is not expected to have material impact on ANSYS' consolidated financial statements in either 2019 or 2020.\n"}{'symbol': 'ANTM', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Anthem Reports Third Quarter 2019 Results', 'text': 'ANTHEM REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.55.Q3 REVENUE $26.4 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $25.9 BILLION.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.87.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $4.82 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FULL YEAR ADJUSTED NET INCOME IS NOW EXPECTED TO BE GREATER THAN $19.40* PER SHARE..COMPANY NOW EXPECTS FULL YEAR NET INCOME TO BE GREATER THAN $18.45 PER SHARE..Q4 2019 DIVIDEND OF $0.80 PER SHARE DECLARED TO SHAREHOLDERS.MEDICAL ENROLLMENT TOTALED APPROXIMATELY 41.0 MILLION MEMBERS AT SEPT 30, 2019, AN INCREASE OF 1.1 MILLION, OR 2.7 PERCENT, FROM SEPT 30, 2018.BENEFIT EXPENSE RATIO WAS 87.2 PERCENT IN Q3 OF 2019, AN INCREASE OF 240 BASIS POINTS FROM 84.8 PERCENT IN PRIOR YEAR QUARTER.FY 2019 OPERATING REVENUE IS NOW EXPECTED TO BE APPROXIMATELY $103.0 BILLION, INCLUDING PREMIUM REVENUE OF $94.0 BILLION TO $95.0 BILLION.FOR FULL YEAR 2019, CO CONTINUES TO EXPECT UNDERLYING LOCAL GROUP MEDICAL COST TREND WILL BE IN RANGE OF 6.0% PLUS/MINUS 50 BASIS POINTS.FY 2019 BENEFIT EXPENSE RATIO IS NOW EXPECTED TO BE IN RANGE OF 86.5% TO 86.8%.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $19.35, REVENUE VIEW $101.87 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'AON', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Aon plc Appoints Lisa Stevens as Chief People Officer', 'text': "Aon plc announced the appointment of Lisa Stevens as Chief People Officer, part of an ongoing series of actions to further strengthen alignment and accelerate momentum in bringing its Aon United growth strategy closer to clients around the world. Since joining Aon in December 2018, Stevens has been a key leader as the firm has established the framework for its Delivering Aon United program, a cornerstone component of the growth strategy now propelling Aon forward. As Chief People Officer, Stevens will build upon the work that has been done by Aon's Human Resources leadership team to refine the path and define the next-generation colleague engagement and culture strategy as the firm continues to evolve, driven by a commitment to ensuring clients experience the same globally excellent standard of service in each local market. Stevens joined Aon just under a year ago from Wells Fargo where she was a 29-year veteran leading the Western region of the United States, which included a 32,000-person team spanning 2,700 branches across 24 states. She also served as the executive advisor for the company's Pride team member network on the Enterprise Diversity & Inclusion Committee and as an inaugural member of the Enterprise Environmental Advisory Committee. She is currently an active board member of several nonprofit organizations, including Arizona State University'sGlobal Institute of Sustainability. As part of this process, Aon worked with Mattson and Company, a boutique consulting firm specializing in C-level and Board searches, to conduct a comprehensive, global search to identify the right candidate for this role."}{'symbol': 'APTV', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Aptiv PLC Declares Quarterly Dividend, Payable on November 20, 2019', 'text': 'Aptiv PLC announced that its Board of Directors declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.22 per ordinary share, payable on November 20, 2019, to shareholders of record at the close of business on November 6, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'AJG', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Arthur J. Gallagher & Co. Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Arthur J. Gallagher & Co. Announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced total revenue was USD 1,825.2 million compared to USD 1,778.5 million a year ago. Net income was USD 126.1 million compared to USD 127.6 million a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 0.66 compared to USD 0.68 a year ago. For the nine months, total revenue was USD 5,473.6 million compared to USD 5,276.6 million a year ago. Net income was USD 570.3 million compared to USD 516.2 million a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 3.01 compared to USD 2.78 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'T', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'At&T Inc., Sprint, T-Mobile and Verizon Form Joint Venture to Transform Messaging Experience', 'text': "AT&T, Sprint, T-Mobile and Verizon have created a joint venture - the Cross Carrier Messaging Initiative (CCMI) - to deliver the next generation of messaging to consumers and businesses. The service, based on GSMA's Rich Communications Service (RCS) industry standard, will enable an engaging way for consumers to interact and transact with each other and with businesses. To enable the service, the CCMI joint venture is working to develop and deploy the standards-based, interoperable messaging service starting with Android and expected in 2020. Working with its carrier ownership group and other companies in the RCS ecosystem, the CCMI service will: Drive a robust business-to-consumer messaging ecosystem and accelerate the adoption of Rich Communications Services (RCS); Enable an enhanced experience to privately send individual or group chats across carriers with high quality pictures and videos; Provide consumers with the ability to chat with their favorite brands, order a rideshare, pay bills or schedule appointments, and more; Create a single seamless, interoperable RCS experience across carriers, both in the U.S. and globally."}{'symbol': 'AVY', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Avery Dennison Declares Quarterly Dividend, Payable on December 18, 2019', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Avery Dennison Corporation has declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.58 per share. The dividend is payable on December 18, 2019, to shareholders of record on December 4, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'AVY', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Avery Dennison Reports Q3 Sales Of $1.76 Billion', 'text': 'AVERY DENNISON ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.66.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.71.Q3 SALES $1.76 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.75 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.61 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.50 TO $6.60.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.15 TO $3.25.QTRLY ORGANIC SALES GROWTH (NON-GAAP) OF 2.1%.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $6.52 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.AVERY DENNISON - 2019 ADJUSTED EPS GUIDANCE EXCLUDES ESTIMATED $3.35 PER SHARE RELATED TO PENSION SETTLEMENT CHARGES, RESTRUCTURING CHARGES AND OTHER ITEMS.'}{'symbol': 'BAX', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Baxter International Inc. Provides Sale Guidance for the Fourth Quarter of 2019', 'text': 'Baxter International Inc. provided sale guidance for the fourth quarter of 2019. For the quarter, the company expects sales growth of 3-4% on a reported basis and approximately 5% on a constant currency and operational basis.'}{'symbol': 'BRK-B', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc. Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Berkshire Hathaway Inc. announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 4,338 million compared to USD 4,419 million a year ago. Net income was USD 16,524 million compared to USD 18,540 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 10,119 compared to USD 11,280 a year ago. For the nine months, sales was USD 11,729 million compared to USD 11,818 million a year ago. Net income was USD 52,258 million compared to USD 29,413 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 31,944 compared to USD 17,885 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'BIIB', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Society for Biological Engineering, AfroBiotech Conference 2019, Oct 27, 2019 through Oct 29, 2019', 'text': 'Society for Biological Engineering, AfroBiotech Conference 2019, Oct 27, 2019 through Oct 29, 2019. Venue: Hyatt Centric Midtown Atlanta, Atlanta, Georgia, United States.'}{'symbol': 'BLK', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'BlackRock, Inc. Presents at #from Evolution to REVOLUTION, Nov-14-2019 10:45 AM', 'text': 'BlackRock, Inc. Presents at #from Evolution to REVOLUTION, Nov-14-2019 10:45 AM. Venue: The Broadmoor, Colorado Sprigns, Colorado, United States. Speakers: Baker Vitale.'}{'symbol': 'BSX', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Boston Scientific Reports Q3 GAAP Earnings Per Share Of $0.09', 'text': 'BOSTON SCIENTIFIC ANNOUNCES RESULTS FOR THIRD QUARTER 2019.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.09.Q3 SALES $2.707 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $2.65 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.38 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES Q4 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.42 TO $0.45 EXCLUDING ITEMS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.39.SEES REVENUE GROWTH FOR FULL YEAR 2019 TO BE IN A RANGE OF APPROXIMATELY 9 TO 9.5 PERCENT ON A REPORTED BASIS.SEES REVENUE GROWTH FOR FULL YEAR 2019 TO BE IN A RANGE OF APPROXIMATELY 7.5 PERCENT ON AN ORGANIC BASIS.BOSTON SCIENTIFIC - QTRLY CARDIOVASCULAR NET SALES $1,011 MILLION, UP 11.3%.SEES 2019 INCOME ON A GAAP BASIS IN A RANGE OF $0.72 TO $0.75 PER SHARE.SEES 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS IN A RANGE OF $1.55 TO $1.58 PER SHARE.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.44 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.56, REVENUE VIEW $10.70 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'BMY', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Bristol-Myers Squibb Company Announces the Approval of Opdivo (Nivolumab) Four-Week Dosing Schedule for the Adjuvant Treatment of Adult Patients with Melanoma with Involvement of Lymph Nodes or Metastatic Disease', 'text': 'Bristol-Myers Squibb Company announced that the European Commission (EC) has approved Opdivo (nivolumab) flat dosing schedule of 240 mg infused over 30 minutes every two weeks (Q2W) or 480 mg infused over 60 minutes every four weeks (Q4W) for the adjuvant treatment of adult patients with melanoma with involvement of lymph nodes or metastatic disease who have undergone complete resection. Opdivo is a programmed death-1 (PD-1) immune checkpoint inhibitor that is designed to uniquely harness the body’s own immune system to help restore anti-tumor immune response. By harnessing the body’s own immune system to fight cancer, Opdivo has become an important treatment option across multiple cancers. Melanoma is separated into five staging categories (Stages 0- IV) based on the in-situ feature, thickness and ulceration of the tumor, whether the cancer has spread to the lymph nodes, and how far the cancer has spread beyond lymph nodes. Stage III melanoma has generally reached the regional lymph nodes but has not yet spread to distant lymph nodes or to other parts of the body (metastasized) and requires surgical resection of the primary tumor as well as the involved lymph nodes. Some patients may also be treated with adjuvant therapy. Despite surgical intervention, most patients experience disease recurrence and progress to metastatic disease.'}{'symbol': 'COG', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cabot Oil & Gas Corporation Announces Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on November 15, 2019', 'text': "The Board of Directors of Cabot Oil & Gas Corporation has approved an 11% increase in its quarterly cash dividend to $0.10 per share on the Company's common stock, resulting in the fifth dividend increase since May 2017. The dividend will be paid on November 15, 2019 to all shareholders of record as of the close of business on November 6, 2019."}{'symbol': 'CDNS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cadence Design Systems, Inc. Presents at 6th Annual Bernstein Technology Innovation Summit, Nov-06-2019 10:40 AM', 'text': 'Cadence Design Systems, Inc. Presents at 6th Annual Bernstein Technology Innovation Summit, Nov-06-2019 10:40 AM. Venue: The Westin New York at Times Square, 270 west 43rd street, New York, New York, United States. Speakers: Nimish H. Modi, Senior Vice President of Marketing & Business Development.'}{'symbol': 'COF', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Capital One Financial Corporation Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Capital One Financial Corporation announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced net interest income was USD 5,737 million compared to USD 5,786 million a year ago. Net income was USD 1,333 million compared to USD 1,502 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 2.7 compared to USD 3.01 a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 2.71 compared to USD 3.01 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 2.68 compared to USD 2.99 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 2.69 compared to USD 2.99 a year ago. For the nine months, net interest income was USD 17,274 million compared to USD 17,055 million a year ago. Net income was USD 4,370 million compared to USD 4,754 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 8.8 compared to USD 9.4 a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 8.83 compared to USD 9.39 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share from continuing operations was USD 8.76 compared to USD 9.33 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 8.79 compared to USD 9.32 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'KMX', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'CarMax, Inc. Announces Executive Changes', 'text': 'CarMax, Inc. announced, as part of a long-term planning process, its CFO transition. Enrique Mayor-Mora, who has served as CarMax’s treasurer since 2016, will be promoted to senior vice president and CFO. Tom Reedy, who has served as CFO since 2010 and as executive vice president since 2012, will become executive vice president of finance. Mayor-Mora will continue to report to Reedy. The Company noted that Mayor-Mora will assume responsibilities for Accounting, Tax, Treasury, Expansion Planning and Analysis, Financial Planning and Internal Audit functions. Reedy will continue to oversee the CarMax Auto Finance, Financial Services and Products, Investor Relations, Store Delivery and Support Systems, and Real Estate teams.'}{'symbol': 'CERN', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cerner Corporation Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter of 2019', 'text': 'Cerner Corporation provided earnings guidance for the fourth quarter of 2019. For the quarter, the company expects revenue between $1.410 billion and $1.460 billion.'}{'symbol': 'SCHW', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'iCapital Network® and Schwab Advisor Services™ Expand Custodial Relationship to Improve Alternative Investing Experience', 'text': 'iCapital Network and Schwab Advisor Services announced an expanded relationship in which Schwab will provide shareholder servicing for funds serviced by iCapital. iCapital will be the first platform provider on the Schwab Alternative Investment MarketplaceTM platform introduced on October 24, 2019. The agreement will create an end-to-end, automated alternative investing process for advisors who utilize the Schwab platform. iCapital’s technology allows advisors and their high-net-worth clients to access, review and invest in alternative investments such as private equity and hedge funds at lower minimums than traditionally required, bringing efficiency and a premier advisor experience to the management of alternative investments. Under the new agreement, advisors will be able to view iCapital’s curated menu of alternative funds on the Schwab Alternative Investment Marketplace platform and manage iCapital investments within clients’ Schwab accounts. Advisors will also benefit from direct access to research on funds and strategies, a streamlined investing and reporting process and electronic access to documents associated with clients’ investments.'}{'symbol': 'SCHW', 'date': '2019-10-24 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Charles Schwab Declared Regular Quarterly Cash Dividend Of $0.17 Per Common Share', 'text': 'CHARLES SCHWAB CORP - DECLARED A REGULAR QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND OF $0.17 PER COMMON SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'CINF', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cincinnati Financial Corporation Announces Unaudited Consolidated Earnings Results for the Third Quarter and Nine Months Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Cincinnati Financial Corporation announced unaudited consolidated earnings results for the third quarter and nine months ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced total revenue was USD 1,700 million compared to USD 1,915 million a year ago. Net income was USD 248 million compared to USD 553 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.51 compared to USD 3.4 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 1.49 compared to USD 3.38 a year ago. For the nine months, total revenue was USD 5,772 million compared to USD 4,697 million a year ago. Net income was USD 1,371 million compared to USD 739 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 8.4 compared to USD 4.53 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 8.3 compared to USD 4.49 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'C', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Citigroup Inc. has announced a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of €29 million.', 'text': 'Citigroup Inc. has announced a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of €29 million.\n\nSecurity Name: Zero Coupon Senior Notes due October 29, 2049\nSecurity Type: Corporate Bond/Note (Non Convertible)\nPrincipal Amount: €29 million\nPrice\\Range: 100%\nDiscount Per Security: 0%\nSecurity Features: Callable; Global MTN; MTN; Zero Coupon\nCoupon Type: Zero\n\nTransaction Features: Regulation S'}{'symbol': 'CTXS', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Citrix Systems Reports Quarterly Adjusted EPS Of $1.52', 'text': 'CITRIX REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS AND HOSTS FINANCIAL ANALYST MEETING.QUARTERLY GAAP DILUTED EPS OF $2.04 AND NON-GAAP DILUTED EPS OF $1.52.SEES FY 2019 REVENUE $2.99 BILLION TO $3.01 BILLION.SEES FY 2019 GAAP EPS $4.45 TO $4.67.SEES FY 2019 NON-GAAP EPS $5.60 TO $5.70.SEES FY 2020 REVENUE GROWTH 3% TO 4%.SEES FY 2020 GAAP DILUTED EPS $3.34 TO $3.54.SEES FY 2020 NON-GAAP DILUTED EPS $5.25 TO $5.45.QUARTERLY TOTAL NET REVENUES $732.9 MILLION VERSUS $732.5 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.25, REVENUE VIEW $715.3 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $5.48, REVENUE VIEW $2.99 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $6.07, REVENUE VIEW $3.12 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'CTXS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Citrix Systems, Inc. Announces Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on December 20, 2019', 'text': 'On October 24, 2019, Citrix Systems, Inc. announced that its Board of Directors declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.35 per share. This dividend is payable on December 20, 2019 to all shareholders of record at the close of business on December 6, 2019. Future dividends will be subject to Board approval.'}{'symbol': 'CMS', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'CMS Energy Reports Q3 Earnings Of $0.73 Per Share', 'text': 'CMS ENERGY ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER EARNINGS OF $0.73 PER SHARE, INTRODUCES 2020 EARNINGS GUIDANCE AND NEW $25 BILLION 10-YEAR CAPITAL PLAN.REAFFIRMS FY 2019 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.47 TO $2.51.SEES FY 2020 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.63 TO $2.68.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.73.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.67 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.REAFFIRMED ITS GUIDANCE FOR 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS OF $2.47 - $2.51 PER SHARE.INTRODUCES 2020 EARNINGS GUIDANCE AND NEW $25 BILLION 10-YEAR CAPITAL PLAN.QTRLY OPERATING REVENUE $1,546 MILLION VERSUS $1,599 MILLION.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.68 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $1.64 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'CMS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Cms Energy Corp. Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'CMS Energy Corp. announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 1,546 million compared to USD 1,599 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 351 million compared to USD 294 million a year ago. Net income was USD 207 million compared to USD 169 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.73 compared to USD 0.6 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 0.73 compared to USD 0.59 a year ago. For the nine months, sales was USD 5,050 million compared to USD 5,044 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 928 million compared to USD 912 million a year ago. Net income was USD 513 million compared to USD 549 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.81 compared to USD 1.95 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 1.81 compared to USD 1.94 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'CMCSA', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Comcast Reports Qtrly Adjusted Earnings Per Share $0.79', 'text': 'COMCAST - QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.70; QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.79.COMCAST - QTRLY REPORTED REVENUE $26.83 BILLION, UP 21.2%.COMCAST - QTRLY COMCAST CABLE COMMUNICATIONS REPORTED REVENUE $14.58 BILLION, UP 4%.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.75, REVENUE VIEW $26.77 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.COMCAST - QTRLY COMCAST CABLE COMMUNICATIONS TOTAL CUSTOMER RELATIONSHIPS ADDITIONS OF 309,000, UP 3.3%.COMCAST - QTRLY NBCUNIVERSAL REPORTED REVENUE $8.30 BILLION, DOWN 3.5%.COMCAST - QTRLY COMCAST CABLE COMMUNICATIONS AVERAGE TOTAL REVENUE PER CUSTOMER RELATIONSHIP $156.72, UP 0.6%.COMCAST - QTRLY SKY REVENUE ON PRO FORMA BASIS $4.55 BILLION, DOWN 4.2%.COMCAST - QTRLY SKY CUSTOMER RELATIONSHIPS LOSSES ON PRO FORMA BASIS OF 99,000 VERSUS ADDITIONS OF 426,000.'}{'symbol': 'CMCSA', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Comcast Corporation Declares Quarterly Dividend, Payable on January 29, 2020', 'text': 'Comcast Corporation announced that its Board of Directors declared a quarterly dividend of $0.21 a share on the company’s common stock. The quarterly dividend is payable on January 29, 2020 to shareholders of record as of the close of business on January 8, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'DHR', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Danaher Q3 Adjusted Non-GAAP Earnings Per Share $1.16', 'text': 'DANAHER REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.74 TO $4.77.SEES Q4 2019 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.32 TO $1.35.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.38 TO $3.41.SEES Q4 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.06 TO $1.09.Q3 ADJUSTED NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.16.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.89.Q3 REVENUE $5.0 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $5.02 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.15 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.DANAHER - BOTH GAAP AND NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE FIGURES INCLUDE DILUTION FROM 19.4% NON-CONTROLLING INTEREST OF ENVISTA COMPANY NO LONGER OWNS.'}{'symbol': 'DHR', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Danaher Corp. Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 27, 2019', 'text': 'Danaher Corp. announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 27, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 5,037.3 million compared to USD 4,853.1 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 834.8 million compared to USD 830.7 million a year ago. Net income was USD 668 million compared to USD 663.7 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 0.9 compared to USD 0.95 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 0.89 compared to USD 0.93 a year ago. For the nine months, sales was USD 15,073.8 million compared to USD 14,529.5 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 2,442.4 million compared to USD 2,441.2 million a year ago. Net income was USD 1,733.1 million compared to USD 1,904.1 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 2.36 compared to USD 2.72 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 2.32 compared to USD 2.68 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'DVA', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'DaVita Inc., Q3 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 05, 2019', 'text': 'DaVita Inc., Q3 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 05, 2019'}{'symbol': 'DAL', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Delta Air Lines, Inc. (NYSE:DAL) acquired 4.3% stake in Hanjin Transportation Co., Ltd. (KOSE:A002320).', 'text': 'Delta Air Lines, Inc. (NYSE:DAL) acquired 4.3% stake in Hanjin Transportation Co., Ltd. (KOSE:A002320) in June 2019.\nDelta Air Lines, Inc. (NYSE:DAL) completed the acquisition of 4.3% stake in Hanjin Transportation Co., Ltd. (KOSE:A002320) in June 2019.\n'}{'symbol': 'XRAY', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'DENTSPLY SIRONA Inc., Q3 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 07, 2019', 'text': 'DENTSPLY SIRONA Inc., Q3 2019 Earnings Call, Nov 07, 2019'}{'symbol': 'DOW', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dow Q3 Sales $10.8 Billion Versus Refinitiv IBES Estimate Of $10.74 Billion', 'text': 'DOW REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 SALES $10.8 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $10.74 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.73, REVENUE VIEW $10.74 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY EQUITY LOSSES WERE $44 MILLION, COMPARED TO PRO FORMA EQUITY EARNINGS OF $135 MILLION IN YEAR-AGO PERIOD.'}{'symbol': 'DOW', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Dow Inc. Reports Unaudited Consolidated Earnings Results for the Three Months and Consolidated and Proforma Earnings Results for the Nine Months Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Dow Inc. reported unaudited consolidated earnings results for the three and nine months ended September 30, 2019. For the three months, the company reported net sales of $10,764 million against $12,634 million a year ago. Interest income was $19 million against $22 million a year ago. Net income was $347 million against $1,049 million a year ago. Earnings per share basic were $0.45 against $1.36 a year ago.For the nine months, the company reported net sales of $32,747 million against $37,660 million a year ago. Interest income was $58 million against $60 million a year ago. Net income was $1,038 million against $3,852 million a year ago. Earnings per share basic were $1.29 against $5.02 a year ago.For the nine months on proforma basis, the company reported net sales of $32,794 million against $37,844 million a year ago. Interest income was $59 million against $60 million a year ago. Net income from continuing operations available for company common stockholders was $584 million against $2,475 million a year ago. Earnings per share basic from continuing operations were $0.78 against $3.31 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'DD', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Dupont's Dupont Advanced Printing Launches New Pigment Inks at Printing United in Dallas", 'text': 'DuPont Advanced Printing will be displaying its newest ink offerings for the growing digital textile market segment at Printing United Oct. 23-25 at the Kay Bailey Hutchison Convention Center in Dallas, Texas. At the show, DuPont will showcase its new DuPont Artistri P2700 pigment ink designed for roll-to-roll printing. Artistri P2700 is a medium viscosity ink that delivers excellent color saturation, soft hand feel and unmatched wet and dry crock fastness. For Direct-to-Garment (DTG) printers, DuPont is highlighting innovative pretreatment technology which enables stain-free printing and superior hand feel on cotton/polyester blends. And with new choices of gamut expanding colors as wells as its new Color Series E, F and G pigment ink offerings for DTG printing, DuPont continues to offer the most complete and highest performance DTG ink.'}{'symbol': 'EMN', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Eastman Chemical Company Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter of 2019', 'text': 'Eastman Chemical Company provided sales guidance for the fourth quarter of 2019. The company is now expecting lower sales volume and lower capacity utilization in the fourth quarter. The company expects earnings to moderate due to normal seasonality, albeit from a lower base, due to the slower economy.'}{'symbol': 'EBAY', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ebay Inc Reports Third Quarter 2019 Results', 'text': 'THREE-YEAR PLAN TO IMPROVE MARGINS AND REINVEST IN CUSTOMER INITIATIVES.QTRLY GAAP AND NON-GAAP EPS PER DILUTED SHARE OF $0.37 AND $0.67, RESPECTIVELY.QTRLY GAAP AND NON-GAAP EPS PER DILUTED SHARE OF $0.37 AND $0.67.Q3 REVENUE $2.6 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $2.64 BILLION.IN Q3, EBAY GREW ACTIVE BUYERS BY 4% ACROSS ITS PLATFORMS, FOR A TOTAL OF 183 MILLION GLOBAL ACTIVE BUYERS.QTRLY GROSS MERCHANDISE VOLUME (GMV) OF $21.7 BILLION, WAS DOWN 4% ON AN AS-REPORTED BASIS.MARKETPLACE PLATFORMS DELIVERED $2.1 BILLION OF REVENUE AND $20.5 BILLION OF GMV IN QUARTER.SEES Q4 NET REVENUE BETWEEN $2.77 BILLION AND $2.82 BILLION.CONTINUES TO REVIEW ROLE AND VALUE OF STUBHUB AND CLASSIFIEDS IN ITS PORTFOLIO TO DETERMINE BEST PATH FORWARD.QTRLY MARKETPLACE REVENUE WAS DOWN 1% ON AN AS-REPORTED BASIS.ANTICIPATES SHARING  UPDATE ON STUBHUB BUSINESS BEFORE NEXT EARNINGS RELEASE..SEES Q4 GAAP EARNINGS PER DILUTED SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS IN RANGE OF $0.55 - $0.60.GAAP OPERATING MARGIN DECREASED TO 20.1% FOR Q3 OF 2019, COMPARED TO 21.0%.SEES Q4 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER DILUTED SHARE FROM CONTINUING OPERATIONS IN RANGE OF $0.73 - $0.76.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.64 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.NON-GAAP OPERATING MARGIN INCREASED TO 26.6% IN Q3 OF 2019, COMPARED TO 26.4%.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.76, REVENUE VIEW $2.85 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'ECL', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ecolab Inc. Receives U.S. Environmental Protection Agency Approval for Its Oxycide™ Daily Disinfectant Cleaner for Efficacy Against Candida Auris', 'text': 'Ecolab Inc. has received U.S. Environmental Protection Agency (EPA) approval for its OxyCide™ Daily Disinfectant Cleaner for efficacy against Candida auris (C. auris), an emerging fungal pathogen that presents a serious global health threat. According to the U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC), C. auris is difficult to identify, multi-drug resistant and can spread through sick patients as well as on contaminated surfaces and equipment, putting hospitalized patients and hospital systems at risk for outbreaks. C. auris has been cultured from multiple locations in patient rooms, including both high touch surfaces, such as bedside tables and bedrails, and locations further away from the patient. C. auris has also been identified on mobile equipment, such as glucometers, temperature probes, blood pressure cuffs, ultrasound machines, nursing carts and crash carts. OxyCide Daily Disinfectant Cleaner is an EPA-registered one-step disinfectant cleaner, virucide and deodorizer with sporicidal activity designed for daily hospital use on both flexible and hard non-porous surfaces. When used as directed, it is proven effective in preventing healthcare-associated infections (HAIs); killing C. auris in three minutes as well as Clostridioidesdifficile (C. diff) and 32 other organisms in five minutes or less.'}{'symbol': 'EIX', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Carey A. Smith Joins Edison International and Southern California Edison’s Boards of Directors', 'text': 'Edison International and Southern California Edison announced that Carey A. Smith has been elected to the board of directors of each company, effective Oct. 24, 2019. Smith is COO at Parsons Corporation. Previously, Smith served in progressive leadership roles at Honeywell, including president of its defense andspace division, vice president of Honeywell Aerospace customer and product support and president of Honeywell Technology Solutions Inc. Smith serves on the board of the Professional Services Council and will continue on the board of NN Inc. until Nov. 14.'}{'symbol': 'EW', 'date': '2019-10-24 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Edwards Lifesciences \u200d\u200bQ3 Adjusted EPS $1.41', 'text': '\u200d\u200bQ3 SALES GREW 21% TO $1.1 BILLION.\u200d\u200bQ3 EPS $1.30; Q3 ADJUSTED EPS $1.41.\u200d\u200bQ3 TAVR SALES OF $700 MILLION, UP 26 PERCENT.\u200d\u200b2019 ADJUSTED EPS GUIDANCE RAISED TO $5.50 TO $5.65 FROM $5.20 TO $5.40.'}{'symbol': 'EW', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Edwards Lifesciences Reports Third Quarter Results', 'text': 'EDWARDS LIFESCIENCES REPORTS THIRD QUARTER RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.41.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.30.Q3 SALES $1.1 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.04 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.22 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FOR 2019, COMPANY NOW EXPECTS TOTAL SALES AROUND TOP OF ITS PREVIOUS $4.0 BILLION TO $4.3 BILLION RANGE.FOR QUARTER, COMPANY REPORTED TAVR SALES OF $700 MILLION, AN INCREASE OF 26 PERCENT OVER Q3 LAST YEAR.RAISED ITS FULL YEAR 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE GUIDANCE TO $5.50 TO $5.65.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $5.34, REVENUE VIEW $4.23 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'ENPH', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Enphase Energy, Inc. Enables Public Service Solar to Deliver A Better Customer Experience', 'text': 'Enphase Energy, Inc. announced that Public Service Solar, a leading residential solar installation company serving New Jersey and Pennsylvania, uses Enphase products to speed up solar installations, allowing the company’s representatives more time to train their customers on the operations and benefits of their Enphase-based solar systems. Public Service Solar serves homeowners in New Jersey and Pennsylvania by delivering a holistic customer experience, from first contact and the sale to final installation and throughout the life of the solar system. The company uses the Enphase IQ™ home energy platform to provide its customers with solar systems that are less prone to production losses from shading due to Enphase’s resilient, distributed architecture and great reliability. Public Service Solar customers also benefit from Enphase’s microinverter systems because they can be right-sized for individual homes since they are not bound to the strict sizing requirements of conventional string-inverter-based systems.'}{'symbol': 'EFX', 'date': '2019-10-24 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Equifax Reports Q3 Earnings Per Share Of $0.66', 'text': 'Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.48.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.66.Q3 REVENUE ROSE 5 PERCENT TO $875.7 MILLION.FOR Q4 OF 2019, EXPECT REPORTED REVENUE TO BE BETWEEN $885 AND $900 MILLION.SEES Q4 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.47 TO $1.52.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.44, REVENUE VIEW $871.2 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES Q4 2019 REVENUE $885 MILLION TO $900 MILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.55, REVENUE VIEW $882.2 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ADJUSTED REVENUE WAS $895.7 MILLION IN Q3, UP 7 PERCENT COMPARED TO Q3 OF 2018.'}{'symbol': 'ESS', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Essex Announces Third Quarter 2019 Results', 'text': 'ESSEX ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.SEES FY 2019 FFO PER SHARE $13.50 TO $13.60.SEES Q4 FFO PER SHARE $3.31 TO $3.41.SEES Q4 2019 CORE FFO PER SHARE $3.36 TO $3.46.QTRLY CORE FFO PER SHARE $3.35.RAISED FULL-YEAR CORE FFO PER DILUTED SHARE GUIDANCE BY $0.05 PER SHARE AT MIDPOINT TO A RANGE OF $13.28 TO $13.38.PROVIDED CORE FFO GUIDANCE RANGE FOR Q4 OF $3.36 TO $3.46 PER DILUTED SHARE.PROVIDED TOTAL FFO GUIDANCE RANGE FOR Q4 OF $3.31 TO $3.41 PER DILUTED SHARE.QTRLY TOTAL FFO PER SHARE $3.50.Q3 FFO PER SHARE VIEW $3.35 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.51.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.34 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'FFIV', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "F5 Networks' Big-IQ Integrated with Venafi Machine Identity Protection Platform for Superior App Security", 'text': 'Venafi announced that F5 Networks has built native integration capabilities for the Venafi Machine Identity Protection Platform into the F5 BIG-IQ Centralized Management solution. The new native Venafi integration with BIG-IQ helps protect organizations by allowing network operations to orchestrate the entire lifecycle of SSL/TLS certificates, scale the process at DevOps speed and ensure security policies are enforced across F5 devices. F5 BIG-IQ Centralized Management offers organizations complete lifecycle management for BIG-IP application services and devices—enabling them to provide the availability, performance and security necessary to achieve digital transformation goals. With the latest release of BIG-IQ, enterprises can orchestrate and inject automation into the process of assigning and managing TLS keys with the Venafi Platform, removing the complexity of TLS key and certificate usage. BIG-IQ customers can connect to more than 40 certificate authorities (CAs) supported by the Venafi Platform. In addition, security policies are enforced without slowing BIG-IP operations.'}{'symbol': 'FFIV', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'F5 Networks Announces Q4 Non-Gaap Earnings Per Share $2.59', 'text': 'F5 NETWORKS ANNOUNCES FOURTH QUARTER AND FISCAL YEAR 2019 RESULTS; DELIVERS SECOND CONSECUTIVE QUARTER OF 91% SOFTWARE REVENUE GROWTH.Q4 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.59.Q4 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.57.SEES Q1 2020 REVENUE $560 MILLION TO $570 MILLION.Q4 REVENUE $590.4 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $582.4 MILLION.Q4 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.55 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES Q1 2020 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.41 TO $2.44.Q1 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $2.47, REVENUE VIEW $566.7 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'FIS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'FIS Announces Quarterly Dividend, Payable on December 27, 2019', 'text': 'FIS announced a regular quarterly dividend of $0.35 per common share. The dividend is payable on December 27, 2019, to shareholders of record as of close of business on December 13, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'FISV', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Fiserv, Inc. Presents at Fifth annual conference, CONVERGE, Nov-06-2019', 'text': 'Fiserv, Inc. Presents at Fifth annual conference, CONVERGE, Nov-06-2019 . Venue: New York Stock Exchange, New york, New York, United States. Speakers: Kamesh Tumsi, VP of Product Strategy.'}{'symbol': 'F', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Ford Motor Company Reports Unaudited Consolidated Financial Results for the Third Quarter and Nine Months Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Ford Motor Company reported unaudited consolidated financial results for the third quarter and nine months ended September 30, 2019. For the quarter, total revenues were $36,990 million against $37,666 million reported a year ago. Operating loss was $261 million against income of $864 million reported a year ago. Net income was $423 million against $993 million reported a year ago. Basic income per share is $0.11 against $0.25 reported a year ago.For the nine months, total revenues were $116,185 million against $118,545 million reported a year ago. Operating income was $1,031 million against $2,571 million reported a year ago. Net income was $1,756 million against $3,807 million reported a year ago. Basic income per share is $0.43 against $0.95 reported a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'FTV', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Fortive Corporation Reports Unaudited Consolidated Earnings Results for the Third Quarter and Nine Months Ended September 27, 2019; Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter and Full Year Ending December 31, 2019', 'text': "Fortive Corporation reported unaudited consolidated earnings results for the third quarter and nine months ended September 27, 2019. For the quarter, the company's sales were $1,860.0 million compared to $1,601.2 million a year ago. Operating profit was $242.1 million compared to $281.6 million a year ago. Net earnings was $207.1 million compared to $245.3 million a year ago. Net earnings per share from continuing operations - basic was $0.57 compared to $0.56 a year ago. Net earnings per share from continuing operations - diluted was $0.56 compared to $0.55 a year ago. Net earnings per share -basic was $0.56 compared to $0.65 a year ago. Net earnings per share -diluted was $0.56 compared to $0.64 a year ago.For the nine months, the company's sales were $5,317.6 million compared to $4,695.2 million a year ago. Operating profit was $708.9 million compared to $883.9 million a year ago. Net earnings was $546.1 million compared to $801.5 million a year ago. Net earnings per share from continuing operations - basic was $1.47 compared to $1.89 a year ago. Net earnings per share from continuing operations - diluted was $1.46 compared to $1.86 a year ago. Net earnings per share -basic was $1.47 compared to $2.24 a year ago. Net earnings per share -diluted was $1.46 compared to $2.21 a year ago.The company also provided earnings guidance for the fourth quarter and full year ending December 31, 2019. For the quarter, the company's diluted net earnings per share from continuing operations attributable to common stockholders is expected to be between $0.36 to $0.41. For the year, the company's diluted net earnings per share from continuing operations attributable to common stockholders is expected to be between $1.81 to $1.86."}{'symbol': 'FBHS', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Fortune Brands Home & Security Reports Q3 Earnings Per Share Of $0.75', 'text': 'FORTUNE BRANDS REPORTS Q3 2019 SALES AND EPS GROWTH; SOLID PROGRESS ON STRATEGIC INITIATIVES IN A SLOWLY RECOVERING HOUSING MARKET.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.75.Q3 SALES $1.46 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $1.49 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.95 EXCLUDING ITEMS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.98 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.TIGHTENS 2019 OUTLOOK FOR SALES GROWTH TO 5 TO 6 PERCENT AND EPS BEFORE CHARGES/GAINS TO $3.53 - $3.63.EXPECTS TO GENERATE FREE CASH FLOW OF ABOUT $480 MILLION TO $500 MILLION FOR FY 2019.'}{'symbol': 'GNRC', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Sofdesk Inc. announced that it has received $5.7 million in funding from Generac Holdings Inc., EnerTech Capital, BDC Capital Inc., Desjardins Capital Inc. and another investor', 'text': 'Sofdesk Inc. announced that it has received $5.7 million in equity round of funding led by new investor Generac Holdings Inc. (NYSE:GNRC) on October 24, 2019. The transaction also involved participation from new investor Desjardins Capital Inc. and returning investor EnerTech Capital and BDC Capital Inc. The company has received $4,359,361 from 5 investors pursuant to exemption provided under Regulation D.'}{'symbol': 'GIS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'General Mills, Inc. Presents at #from Evolution to REVOLUTION, Nov-14-2019 11:40 AM', 'text': 'General Mills, Inc. Presents at #from Evolution to REVOLUTION, Nov-14-2019 11:40 AM. Venue: The Broadmoor, Colorado Sprigns, Colorado, United States. Speakers: Carla Vernon.'}{'symbol': 'GILD', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Gilead Sciences Announces Fourth Quarter 2019 Dividend, Payable on December 30, 2019', 'text': 'Gilead Sciences, Inc. announced that the company’s Board of Directors has declared a cash dividend of $0.63 per share of common stock for the fourth quarter of 2019. The dividend is payable on December 30, 2019, to stockholders of record at the close of business on December 13, 2019. Future dividends will be subject to Board approval.'}{'symbol': 'GL', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Globe Life Reports Third Quarter 2019 Results', 'text': 'Q3 OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.73.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.70 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $6.71 TO $6.77.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.82.PROJECTS THAT NET OPERATING INCOME PER SHARE WILL BE IN RANGE OF $7.00 TO $7.30 FOR YEAR ENDING DECEMBER 31, 2020.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $6.73 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $7.18 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'GS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc. Presents at Financial Institutions Conference 2019: Future Proofing European Banking - Frankfurt, Nov-07-2019 10:00 AM', 'text': 'The Goldman Sachs Group, Inc. Presents at Financial Institutions Conference 2019: Future Proofing European Banking - Frankfurt, Nov-07-2019 10:00 AM. Venue: Steigenberger Frankfurter Hof, Am Kaiserplatz, Bethmannstraße 33, Frankfurt, Germany. Speakers: Alexandre Traub, Co-Head of Securities Germany/Austria.'}{'symbol': 'HSY', 'date': '2019-10-24 12:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hershey Exec - Expect Q4 Gross Margin Expansion To Be Less Than Q3', 'text': "HERSHEY EXEC - $2 BILLION REESE'S BRAND'S RETAIL SALES GREW OVER 6% IN Q3.HERSHEY EXEC - REESE'S, HERSHEY MINIATURES, KISSES AND KIT KAT ARE SEEING NICE LIFTS FROM OUR NEW PACKAGING IN THE TAKE HOME AISLE.HERSHEY EXEC - E-COMMERCE CONFECTION BUSINESS POSTED NET SALES GROWTH OF ABOUT 50% IN Q3, DRIVEN BY STRONG HALLOWEEN SELL-IN.EXEC - ONE BRANDS PORTFOLIO HAS NET SALES OF ABOUT $100 MILLION.HERSHEY EXEC - EXPECT Q4 GROSS MARGIN EXPANSION TO BE LESS THAN THIRD QUARTER.EXEC - EXPECT FY INTEREST EXPENSE OF ABOUT $145 MILLION, THE HIGH END OF  PRIOR RANGE DUE TO RECENT ACQUISITION OF ONE BRANDS.EXEC - GIVEN ACQUISITION-RELATED COSTS, WE EXPECT IT TO BE SLIGHTLY DILUTIVE TO REPORTED EARNINGS & HAVE A NEGLIGIBLE IMPACT TO ADJUSTED PROFIT IN Q4.HERSHEY EXEC - Q3 ORGANIC CONSTANT CURRENCY NET SALES GROWTH DRIVEN PRIMARILY BY PRICING IN NORTH AMERICA & VOLUME GROWTH IN INTERNATIONAL.HERSHEY EXEC - COCOA PRICES TODAY VERSUS LAST 12 TO 24 MONTHS, THEY'RE HIGHER, SO AT MINIMUM, WE'RE NOT LIKELY TO HAVE A TAILWIND IN 2020.HERSHEY EXEC - BRAZIL MARKET IS CHALLENGED GIVEN COMBINATION OF MACROECONOMIC AND COMPETITIVE ACTIVITY AROUND DEEP DISCOUNTING."}{'symbol': 'HSY', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hershey Posts Q3 Earnings Per Share $1.54', 'text': "HERSHEY REPORTS THIRD-QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS; UPDATES 2019 NET SALES OUTLOOK FOR THE ACQUISITION OF ONE BRANDS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.54.Q3 SALES ROSE 2.6 PERCENT TO $2.134 BILLION.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $5.68 TO $5.74.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $5.54 TO $5.66.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.61.SEES FY 2019 SALES UP ABOUT 2.5 PERCENT.PLEASED WITH OUR THIRD-QUARTER RESULTS AND MOMENTUM WE ARE SEEING IN OUR CORE BUSINESS.AMPLIFY PORTFOLIO CONTINUES TO DELIVER MID- TO HIGH-SINGLE-DIGIT GROWTH.CONTINUE TO EXECUTE AGAINST OUR BROADER SNACKING AMBITION.NET IMPACT OF DEALS ON QTRLY NET SALES WAS A 1.2 POINT BENEFIT, WHILE FOREIGN CURRENCY EXCHANGE WAS A 0.2 POINT HEADWIND.SEES 2019 IMPACT OF FOREIGN CURRENCY EXCHANGE ANTICIPATED TO BE SLIGHTLY NEGATIVE BASED ON CURRENT EXCHANGE RATES.HERSHEY'S NORTH AMERICA NET SALES WERE $1,894.0 MILLION IN Q3 OF 2019, AN INCREASE OF 2.7% VERSUS SAME PERIOD LAST YEAR.UPDATED 2019 NET SALES OUTLOOK TO REFLECT THE ACQUISITION OF ONE BRANDS LLC.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.60, REVENUE VIEW $2.12 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $5.76, REVENUE VIEW $7.95 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA."}{'symbol': 'HSY', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hershey Company Declares Quarterly Dividends, Payable on December 16, 2019', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of The Hershey Company announced quarterly dividends of $0.773 on the Common Stock and $0.702 on the Class B Common Stock. The dividends were declared on October 22, 2019, and are payable on December 16, 2019, to stockholders of record November 22, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'HPE', 'date': '2019-10-24 19:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hewlett Packard Enterprise Announces FY20 Outlook', 'text': 'HEWLETT PACKARD ENTERPRISE OUTLINES AS-A-SERVICE STRATEGY AND ANNOUNCES FY20 OUTLOOK.ESTIMATES FY20 NON-GAAP DILUTED NET EARNINGS PER SHARE OUTLOOK OF $1.78-$1.94,.ESTIMATES FY20 GAAP DILUTED NET EARNINGS PER SHARE OUTLOOK OF $1.01-$1.17.EXPECTS FY20 FREE CASH FLOW OF $1.9 BILLION TO $2.1 BILLION.INCREASES QUARTERLY DIVIDEND TO $0.12 PER SHARE.EXPECTS COMPOUNDED ANNUAL REVENUE GROWTH RATE OF 1-3% ADJUSTED FOR CURRENCY FOR FY19-FY22.EXPECTS COMPOUNDED ANNUAL NON-GAAP OPERATING PROFIT GROWTH RATE OF 5-7% FOR FY19-FY22.EXPECTS CAPITAL DISTRIBUTIONS TO SHAREHOLDERS TO BE BETWEEN 50-75% OF FCF OVER LONG-TERM.HEWLETT PACKARD ENTERPRISE - NON-GAAP NET EPS IS EXPECTED TO GROW AT A HIGHER COMPOUNDED ANNUAL GROWTH RATE OF 7-9% FOR FY19-FY22.FY2020 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.80 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'HLT', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Hilton Reports Third Quarter Results', 'text': 'HILTON REPORTS THIRD QUARTER RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.05.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.00.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.02 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SYSTEM-WIDE COMPARABLE REVPAR INCREASED 0.4 PERCENT ON A CURRENCY NEUTRAL BASIS FOR Q3.FULL YEAR 2019 SYSTEM-WIDE COMPARABLE REVPAR IS EXPECTED TO INCREASE APPROXIMATELY 1.0 PERCENT ON A CURRENCY NEUTRAL BASIS.FULL YEAR 2019 CAPITAL RETURN IS PROJECTED TO BE BETWEEN $1.6 BILLION AND $1.8 BILLION.FULL YEAR NET INCOME IS PROJECTED TO BE BETWEEN $923 MILLION AND $937 MILLION.FULL YEAR ADJUSTED EBITDA IS PROJECTED TO BE BETWEEN $2,285 MILLION AND $2,305 MILLION.FOR FULL YEAR 2020, SYSTEM-WIDE COMPARABLE REVPAR IS EXPECTED TO BE FLAT TO 1.0 PERCENT GROWTH ON A CURRENCY NEUTRAL BASIS.2019 DILUTED EPS, BEFORE SPECIAL ITEMS, IS PROJECTED TO BE BETWEEN $3.16 AND $3.21.2019 DILUTED EPS, ADJUSTED FOR SPECIAL ITEMS, IS PROJECTED TO BE BETWEEN $3.81 AND $3.86.2019 MANAGEMENT AND FRANCHISE FEE REVENUE IS PROJECTED TO INCREASE BETWEEN 7 PERCENT AND 8 PERCENT.2019 NET UNIT GROWTH IS EXPECTED TO BE APPROXIMATELY 6.5 PERCENT.Q4 DILUTED EPS, ADJUSTED FOR SPECIAL ITEMS, IS PROJECTED TO BE BETWEEN $0.91 AND $0.96.Q4 DILUTED EPS, BEFORE SPECIAL ITEMS, IS PROJECTED TO BE BETWEEN $0.74 AND $0.79.Q4 SYSTEM-WIDE COMPARABLE REVPAR IS EXPECTED TO BE ROUGHLY FLAT ON A CURRENCY NEUTRAL BASIS.Q4 MANAGEMENT AND FRANCHISE FEE REVENUE IS PROJECTED TO INCREASE BETWEEN 3 PERCENT AND 5 PERCENT.'}{'symbol': 'HON', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Honeywell Establishes Robotics Innovation Hub For Next Generation Distribution Centers', 'text': "Honeywell announced the creation of Honeywell Robotics, an advanced technology center of excellence focused on innovating and developing artificial intelligence, machine learning, computer vision and advanced robotics for use across supply chains. Based in Pittsburgh, Honeywell Robotics will help shape the warehouse and distribution center of the future, particularly as companies look to automated solutions, software and robotics to deliver increased speed, accuracy and throughput in complex material handling environments. Consumer expectations have caused a seismic shift in supply chain operations. Online purchasing, combined with same- or next-day delivery options, has stressed the labor market to the point of a shortage. Nearly 80% of distribution center operations are still performed manually, according to DHL's Robotics in Logistics Study. With industry growth outpacing the labor pool by a rate of 6 to 1, this growth is creating significant opportunities to automate supply chains. The new center of excellence will be led by Joseph Lui, a robotics leader with expertise in digital data, autonomous technologies and the industrial Internet of Things. He previously served as Director of Industrial IoT and Automation Technologies, Robotics for Amazon. Customers can also benefit from Honeywell's Momentum warehouse execution system, a configurable enterprise software platform that orchestrates equipment, labor and inventory for distribution centers. Momentum can help streamline the deployment and integration of advanced robotics by providing warehouse managers with a single, centralized system to manage their operations and automation technology. The establishment of the robotics center of excellence is the continuation of Honeywell's technology transformation, putting significant investment in partnerships with software vendors, universities, startups and incubators to create new solutions for industrial customers with both simple and complex needs. Honeywell also is collaborating with AI researchers at Carnegie Mellon University's National Robotics Engineering Center to develop breakthrough robotics technologies for distribution centers. The company, through its Honeywell Ventures investment fund, has strategic investments in robotics companies, including Soft Robotics and Attabotics, to help automate complex tasks in dynamic environments to maximize productivity and labor efficiency."}{'symbol': 'HUM', 'date': '2019-10-24 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Humana Sets Quarterly Cash Dividend Of $0.55 Per Share', 'text': 'SETS QUARTERLY CASH DIVIDEND OF $0.55PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'HBAN', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Huntington Bancshares Incorporated Declares Quarterly Cash Dividends on its Common and Preferred Stocks, Payable on January 2, 2020', 'text': "Huntington Bancshares Incorporated that the Board of Directors declared a quarterly cash dividend on the company's common stock of $0.15 per common share, unchanged from the prior quarter. The common stock cash dividend is payable January 2, 2020, to shareholders of record on December 18, 2019.In addition, the Board declared quarterly cash dividends on its four series of preferred stock. The Board declared a quarterly cash dividend on its Floating Rate Series B Non-Cumulative Perpetual Preferred Stock (CUSIP#: 446150500) of $11.75219718 per share (equivalent to $0.2938049 per depositary receipt share). The Board declared a quarterly cash dividend on its 5.875% Series C Non-Cumulative Perpetual Preferred Stock of $14.69 per share (equivalent to $0.36725 per depositary receipt share). The Board declared a quarterly cash dividend on its 6.25% Series D Non-Cumulative Perpetual Preferred Stock of $15.625 per share (equivalent to $0.390625 per depositary receipt share). Finally, the Board declared a quarterly cash dividend on its 5.70% Series E Fixed-to-Floating Rate Non-Cumulative Perpetual Preferred Stock (CUSIP#: 446150 AL8) of $1,425.00 per share (equivalent to $14.25 per depositary receipt share). All four preferred stock cash dividends are payable January 15, 2020, to their respective shareholders of record on January 1, 2020."}{'symbol': 'IDXX', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'IDEXX Laboratories, Inc. Announces Leadership Changes', 'text': "IDEXX Laboratories, Inc. announced that Jonathan Ayers is stepping down as Chairman and a member of the IDEXX management team, effective November 1, 2019. This decision follows Mr. Ayers's previously announced medical leave of absence from IDEXX due to a bicycling accident, where he suffered a spinal cord injury. The IDEXX Board of Directors has appointed Jonathan (Jay) Mazelsky, who has been serving as Interim President and Chief Executive Officer since June 28, 2019, as President and Chief Executive Officer, effective immediately. Mr. Mazelsky has also been elected to the IDEXX Board. Lawrence Kingsley, Lead Director, has been appointed as Independent Chairman of the IDEXX Board, effective November 1, 2019. Mr. Ayers will continue as a member of the IDEXX Board and serve as a Senior Advisor to the Company."}{'symbol': 'ILMN', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Illumina Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fiscal Year 2019', 'text': 'Illumina Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fiscal Year 2019. For the fiscal 2019, the company continues to expect year over year revenue growth of approximately 6%, and now expects GAAP earnings per diluted share attributable to Illumina stockholders of $6.55 to $6.60.'}{'symbol': 'INTC', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Intel Corporation Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter and Revised Earnings Guidance for the Full Year of 2019', 'text': 'Intel Corporation provided earnings guidance for the fourth quarter and revised earnings guidance for the full year of 2019. For the quarter, the company expects GAAP diluted earnings per common share of $1.28.For the year, the company expects GAAP diluted earnings per common share of $4.42. The company raising full-year revenue outlook to $71 billion, up $1.5 billion from July guidance.'}{'symbol': 'IBM', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'IBM Expands Cloud Capabilities in Canada to Unlock Digital Transformation', 'text': "IBM on October 24, 2019, announced an expansion of its global cloud footprint, with plans to launch a new IBM Cloud multizone region (MZR) in Canada by late 2020. The MZR in Canada will add to IBM's existing data center capacity and become IBM's first MZR in the country. This will help Canadian enterprises to securely deploy mission-critical workloads and applications across hybrid cloud environments. Located in Toronto, the new MZR will be designed to provide clients with access to globally consistent IBM public cloud services, from enterprise-grade infrastructure to AI services. The MZR will be designed to increase service availability by minimizing interruptions, so that companies can safely keep their data and workloads up and running. As announced earlier this year by Payments Canada, IBM was selected as the lead technology partner for Canada's new high-value payments system, Lynx. Payments Canada is responsible for the safe and secure operation of Canada's national payments systems, which clear and settle close to $210 billion every business day. IBM is the only cloud provider that can deliver levels of encryption certified up to FIPS 140-2 Level 4 as part of its MZR capability. Canadian clients across industries like Payments Canada will have access to these market leading modernization services that will help them compete on a global level. The Canadian MZR brings even more regional capacity and capability to achieve these efficiencies and is designed to deliver SLAs of 99.99% uptime with a complete portfolio of services, including IBM Watson, blockchain, IoT and analytics."}{'symbol': 'IFF', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'IFF Opens Center of Excellence for Food Service and Seasonings in Carrollton, Texas', 'text': 'IFF opened its Center of Excellence for Food Service and Seasonings in Carrollton, Texas. The new site, located near the Company’s existing facility, greatly expands its ability to provide innovative offerings to its customers and represents a significant investment into its food service strategy, as well as its value-add seasonings and savory solutions. IFF has had a presence in Carrollton since its acquisition of Bush Boake Allen (BBA) in 2000, when the original site catered primarily to more locally-based customers. The former BBA facility will be used as an expanded manufacturing site. With the additional space, equipment, and capabilities, and leveraging its central location, the Company foresees growing its customer base in the US.'}{'symbol': 'JNJ', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Moody's Says J&J's Proposed Opioid Agreement Credit Negative", 'text': "Oct 24  - Moody's::MOODY'S SAYS J&J'S PROPOSED OPIOID AGREEMENT CREDIT NEGATIVE.MOODY'S SAYS J&J'S PROPOSED OPIOID AGREEMENT IS CREDIT NEGATIVE BECAUSE OF ITS ADVERSE EFFECT ON J&J'S CASH BALANCES, FREE CASH FLOW.MOODY'S SAYS THERE IS CURRENTLY NO IMPACT FROM PROPOSED OPIOID AGREEMENT ON J&J'S AAA RATINGS OR THE NEGATIVE OUTLOOK."}{'symbol': 'JPM', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'JPMorgan Chase & Co. has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of AUD 16 million.', 'text': 'JPMorgan Chase & Co. has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of AUD 16 million.\n\nSecurity Name: Zero Coupon Notes due October 24, 2022\nSecurity Type: Corporate Bond/Note (Non Convertible)\nPrincipal Amount: AUD 16 million\nPrice\\Range: 100%\nSecurity Features: Callable; Euro MTN; MTN; Zero Coupon\nCoupon Type: Zero\n\nTransaction Features: Regulation S'}{'symbol': 'JNPR', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Juniper Networks, Inc. Declares Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on December 23, 2019', 'text': 'The Board of Directors of Juniper Networks, Inc. has declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.19 per share to be paid on December 23, 2019 to shareholders of record as of the close of business on December 2, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'KIM', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Kimco Realty Reports Q3 Ffo Per Share $0.35', 'text': 'KIMCO REALTY ANNOUNCES THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED FFO PER SHARE $0.37 EXCLUDING ITEMS.Q3 FFO PER SHARE $0.35.UPDATES 2019 OUTLOOK.SEES FY NAREIT FFO: $1.44 TO $1.46.SEES FY FFO AS ADJUSTED: $1.46 TO $1.47.'}{'symbol': 'KIM', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Kimco Realty Corporation Declares Dividend, Payable on January 15, 2020', 'text': 'Kimco Realty Corporation board of directors declared a quarterly cash dividend of $0.28 per common share, payable on January 15, 2020, to shareholders of record on January 2, 2020.'}{'symbol': 'LHX', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'US Air Force Selects L3Harris Technologies to Develop Space Hub End Cryptographic Unit for Protected Tactical SATCOM Program', 'text': 'The U.S. Air Force has selected L3Harris Technologies to deliver the space hub end cryptographic unit (ECU) for the Protected Tactical SATCOM (PTS) SHIELD program. The Air Force PTS program will implement Protected Tactical Waveform (PTW) over a fully-processed satellite payload, enabling adaptive, anti-jam communications channels, which will provide the level of protection available for tactical U.S. and coalition/international partner warfighting efforts. As the SHIELD contractor, L3Harris will develop an NSA-certified, space-flight qualified, production-ready ECU for future PTS payloads. The L3Harris ECUs will support 13 space-based communications payload hubs that will serve up to 1,800 simultaneous tactical user terminals. L3Harris’ Modular Open System Architecture (MOSA) approach employs standards-based interfaces that minimize the information security boundary and simplify integration for the multiple payload providers. The ECU incorporates L3Harris’ HMV™ Space Cryptographic processor that supports full on-orbit reprogrammability in a low-power, highly extensible design. The MOSA form factor and innovative technical approach also results in a low SWaP solution for substantial cost savings due to reduced payload weight and hardware costs. L3Harris was selected by the U.S. Air Force based on its low-risk innovative solution and extensive experience developing Type 1 hardware for space applications as proven on the AEHF, MUOS and SBIRS programs. The SHIELD solution also benefits from extensive reuse of PTW technology from the PTS Field Demonstration Terminal Program to minimize development risk and support the Air Force’s critical deployment schedule.'}{'symbol': 'LH', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Labcorp Announces Q3 Results And Updates 2019 Guidance', 'text': 'LABCORP ANNOUNCES 2019 THIRD QUARTER RESULTS AND UPDATES 2019 GUIDANCE.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.90.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.25.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.85 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $11.20 TO $11.30.LABCORP - 2019 FREE CASH FLOW GUIDANCE OF $950 MILLION TO $1.05 BILLION, UP 3% TO 13% OVER 2018.LABCORP - Q3 REVENUE OF $2.9 BILLION, UP 3.4% OVER $2.8 BILLION LAST YEAR.LABCORP -  LABCORP DIAGNOSTICS REVENUE FOR QUARTER WAS $1.76 BILLION, AN INCREASE OF 0.4%.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $2.91 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.LABCORP -  COVANCE DRUG DEVELOPMENT REVENUE FOR QUARTER WAS $1.18 BILLION, AN INCREASE OF 8.7%.LABCORP SEES 2019 REVENUE GROWTH OF 1.5% TO 2.0% OVER 2018 REVENUE OF $11.33 BILLION.LABCORP -  COVANCE DRUG DEVELOPMENT BACKLOG AT END OF QUARTER WAS $10.71 BILLION COMPARED TO $10.29 BILLION LAST QUARTER.LABCORP - 2019 REVENUE IN LABCORP DIAGNOSTICS IS EXPECTED TO BE DOWN 1.5% TO DOWN 0.5% AS COMPARED TO 2018 REVENUE OF $7.03 BILLION.LABCORP SEES 2019 REVENUE GROWTH IN COVANCE DRUG DEVELOPMENT OF 5.5% TO 7.5% OVER 2018 REVENUE OF $4.31 BILLION.FY2019 REVENUE VIEW $11.48 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $11.27 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'LH', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Laboratory Corp. of America Holdings Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Laboratory Corp. Of America Holdings announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 2,928.5 million compared to USD 2,831.3 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 339.9 million compared to USD 343.4 million a year ago. Net income was USD 220.7 million compared to USD 318.8 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 2.26 compared to USD 3.14 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 2.25 compared to USD 3.1 a year ago. For the nine months, sales was USD 8,601.4 million compared to USD 8,545.9 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 993.8 million compared to USD 1,018 million a year ago. Net income was USD 596.7 million compared to USD 725.8 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 6.08 compared to USD 7.13 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 6.04 compared to USD 7.04 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'LRCX', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Lam Research Reports Quarterly Non-GAAP Earnings Per Share Of $3.18', 'text': 'ORATION REPORTS FINANCIAL RESULTS FOR THE QUARTER ENDED SEPTEMBER 29, 2019.QUARTERLY REVENUE $2.17 BILLION.QUARTERLY NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.18.QUARTERLY GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $3.09.SEES REVENUE OF $2.5 BILLION PLUS/MINUS $150 MILLION IN DEC. 2019 QUARTER.SEES NET INCOME PER DILUTED SHARE OF $3.71 PLUS/MINUS $0.20 IN DEC. 2019 QUARTER.SEES NON-GAAP NET INCOME PER DILUTED SHARE OF $3.80 PLUS/MINUS $0.20 IN DEC. 2019 QUARTER.'}{'symbol': 'LVS', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Las Vegas Sands Reports Q3 Adjusted Earnings Per Share Of $0.75', 'text': 'LAS VEGAS SANDS REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.75.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.69.Q3 REVENUE $3.25 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $3.28 BILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.75 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.ON A HOLD-NORMALIZED BASIS, QTRLY CONSOLIDATED ADJUSTED PROPERTY EBITDA DECREASED 3.0% TO $1.25 BILLION.IN MACAO, ADJUSTED PROPERTY EBITDA WAS $755 MILLION IN QUARTER.QTRLY CONSOLIDATED ADJUSTED PROPERTY EBITDA WAS $1.28 BILLION, CONSISTENT WITH PRIOR YEAR QUARTER.QTRLY MACAO OPERATIONS NET REVENUE $2,112 MILLION VERSUS $2,152 MILLION.ADDITIONAL TOURISM AND ENTERTAINMENT AMENITIES OF LONDONER MACAO WILL DEBUT THROUGHOUT 2020 AND 2021.LAS VEGAS SANDS -  BOARD APPROVED AN INCREASE IN ANNUAL DIVIDEND FOR 2020 CALENDAR YEAR TO $0.79/SHARE PER QUARTER.LAS VEGAS SANDS - ON A GAAP BASIS QTRLY TOTAL NET REVENUES FOR SANDS CHINA LTD DECREASED 2.0% TO $2.11 BILLION.'}{'symbol': 'LLY', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Lilly Announces Cash Tender Offer for Up to $2.0 Billion Aggregate Principal Amount of its Outstanding Debt Securities', 'text': 'Eli Lilly and Company announced that it has commenced a cash tender offer for up to $2.0 billion aggregate principal amount (the "tender cap") of specified series of its outstanding debt. Pursuant to the tender offer, Lilly is offering to purchase, under certain conditions and subject to certain limitations, its 3.950% Notes due 2047, 3.700% Notes due 2045, 3.875% Notes due 2039, 7.125% Notes due 2025, 6.77% Notes due 2036, 5.950% Notes due 2037, 5.55% Notes due 2037, 5.50% Notes due 2027, 4.650% Notes due 2044, 3.100% Notes due 2027, 2.750% Notes due 2025, 3.375% Notes due 2029, 3.950% Notes due 2049, 4.150% Notes due 2059 and 2.350% Notes due 2022 (collectively, the "notes"). The early tender date is 5:00 p.m., New York City time, on November 6, 2019, unless extended. The expiration date of the tender offer is 11:59 p.m., New York City time, on November 21, 2019, unless extended or earlier terminated. The terms, conditions and limitations of the tender offer are described in the Offer to Purchase dated as of today\'s date. Holders of notes must validly tender and not validly withdraw their notes before the early tender date to be eligible to receive the total consideration. Tendered notes may only be withdrawn prior to 5:00 p.m., New York City time, on November 6, 2019. Notes tendered after the withdrawal date and before the expiration date may not be withdrawn, except in certain limited circumstances where additional withdrawal rights are required by law.'}{'symbol': 'LIN', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Linde plc Declares Dividend for the Third Quarter 2019, Payable on December 17, 2019', 'text': 'Linde plc announced that its Board of Directors has declared a quarterly dividend of $0.875 per share. The dividend is payable on December 17, 2019 to shareholders of record on December 3, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'LIN', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Linde Buys Minority Stake In ITM Power, Agrees Joint Venture', 'text': "LINDE ACQUIRES MINORITY STAKE IN ITM POWER AND AGREES JOINT VENTURE.TRANSACTION PROVIDES LINDE WITH A STRATEGIC INVESTMENT IN A WORLD LEADING MANUFACTURER OF INTEGRATED HYDROGEN ENERGY SOLUTIONS.WILL FORM A JOINT VENTURE WITH ITM POWER TO IMPLEMENT PROJECTS BASED ON ITM POWER'S TECHNOLOGY.IN ADDITION TO ITS INVESTMENT, LINDE WILL FORM A JOINT VENTURE WITH ITM POWER TO IMPLEMENT PROJECTS BASED ON ITM POWER'S TECHNOLOGY.JOINT VENTURE IS EXPECTED TO CREATE CAPACITY TO DELIVER A HIGHER VOLUME OF PROJECTS, SHORTEN LEAD TIMES, IMPROVE EXECUTION AND REDUCE COSTS."}{'symbol': 'LMT', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Lockheed Martin And TRC Reach Definitive Agreement', 'text': "LOCKHEED MARTIN AND TRC REACH DEFINITIVE AGREEMENT.LOCKHEED MARTIN AND TRC REACH DEFINITIVE AGREEMENT.LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP - TRC TO ACQUIRE DISTRIBUTED ENERGY SOLUTIONS BUSINESS.LOCKHEED MARTIN - SALE IS PART OF LOCKHEED MARTIN ENERGY'S STRATEGY TO FOCUS ON PRODUCTS AND TECHNOLOGY FOR ENERGY MARKETPLACE & DEPARTMENT OF DEFENSE."}{'symbol': 'LMT', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Lockheed Martin Awarded Air Force ICBM Contract', 'text': 'LOCKHEED MARTIN AWARDED AIR FORCE ICBM CONTRACT.LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP - POTENTIAL VALUE OF MK21A CONTRACT WORTH $138 MILLION.LOCKHEED MARTIN CORP - $108 MILLION AWARDED IN THREE-YEAR CONTRACT & $30 MILLION AS A POTENTIAL ONE-YEAR CONTRACT.'}{'symbol': 'LOW', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': "Lowe's Companies, Inc. Announces the Retirement of Matthew V. Hollifield as Senior Vice President and Chief Accounting Officer", 'text': "On October 23, 2019, Matthew V. Hollifield announced his intention to retire as Senior Vice President and Chief Accounting Officer of Lowe's Companies, Inc. Mr. Hollifield will remain employed with the Company until December 13, 2019 and will thereafter provide consulting services to the Company through February 2020."}{'symbol': 'MPC', 'date': '2019-10-24 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Paul Foster And Jeff Stevens Issue Open Letter To Marathon Petroleum Corporation’s Stockholders', 'text': 'PAUL FOSTER AND JEFF STEVENS ISSUE OPEN LETTER TO MARATHON PETROLEUM CORPORATION’S STOCKHOLDERS.PAUL FOSTER & JEFF STEVENS - FOUND THERE IS "OVERWHELMING" SUPPORT FOR CALLS TO HAVE MARATHON PETROLEUM CHAIRMAN & CEO GARY HEMINGER RESIGN IMMEDIATELY.PAUL FOSTER & JEFF STEVENS - TOGETHER WITH AFFILIATES, HOLD ABOUT 1.7% OF OUTSTANDING COMMON STOCK OF MARATHON PETROLEUM.PAUL FOSTER & JEFF STEVENS - MEETINGS WITH ABOUT 100 MARATHON PETROLEUM STOCKHOLDERS REVEAL "STRONG DEMAND" FOR ADOPTING MUCH OF ELLIOTT\'S PROPOSAL.PAUL FOSTER & JEFF STEVENS - BELIEVE MPC BOARD MUST IMMEDIATELY ESTABLISH SPECIAL COMMITTEE TO IDENTIFY CANDIDATES FOR CHAIRMAN & CEO POSITIONS.'}{'symbol': 'MKTX', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Marketaxess Holdings Q3 Earnings Per Share $1.42', 'text': 'MARKETAXESS REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RECORD REVENUES OF $131.6 MILLION, RECORD OPERATING INCOME OF $66.0 MILLION AND RECORD DILUTED EPS OF $1.42.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.42.Q3 REVENUE $131.6 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $128 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.39 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 OPERATING EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.42.QTRLY TRADING VOLUME OF $528.7 BILLION, UP 37%.QTRLY OPEN TRADING(TM) VOLUME OF $141.7 BILLION, UP 61%.COMPANY IS RECONFIRMING ITS FULL YEAR 2019 EXPENSE GUIDANCE RANGE OF $244.0 MILLION TO $256.0 MILLION.COMPANY IS UPDATING ITS FULL YEAR 2019 CAPITAL EXPENDITURE GUIDANCE RANGE TO $31.0 MILLION TO $33.0 MILLION.'}{'symbol': 'MA', 'date': '2019-10-24 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Brex And Mastercard Partner On U.S. Expansion', 'text': 'BREX AND MASTERCARD PARTNER ON U.S. EXPANSION.MASTERCARD - BREX MASTERCARD CARDHOLDERS WILL RECEIVE SEGMENT-SPECIFIC BENEFITS IN ADDITION TO CORE BENEFITS OF MASTERCARD WORLD ELITE PROGRAM.'}{'symbol': 'MA', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Brex, Has Partnered with Mastercard as Its Preferred Network to Bring Cutting-Edge Technology and Top-Tier Benefits to Its Corporate Card Portfolio in the United States', 'text': 'Mastercard announced that Brex, has partnered with Mastercard as its preferred network to bring cutting-edge technology and top-tier benefits to its corporate card portfolio in the United States. This is a further investment in a partnership that began earlier this year when Brex started issuing World Elite Mastercard for Business. Under the program, Brex Mastercard cardholders will receive segment-specific benefits in addition to the core benefits of the Mastercard World Elite program. World Elite program benefits will include cell-phone insurance, rental car insurance, and ID theft protection, while the Brex rewards program will provide $50,000 worth of partner offers from AWS, Salesforce, Zoom, and many more. San Francisco-based Brex provides startup founders, ecommerce, and life science companies corporate credit cards that require no personal guarantees, deposits or credit scores. In addition to their card programs, Brex provides easy-to-use financial and expense-management tools for seamless reconciliation. Brex has grown at breakneck pace over the last two years – since it was launched, the company has both identified and solved for challenges that have plagued small businesses and entrepreneurs through access to credit. Mastercard’s technology is industry-leading and will enable Brex to address the needs of an expanding customer base. By working with Mastercard, Brex will leverage the network’s platform innovation to develop new features, rewards, and experiences for its cardholders. Brex card rewards and other functionalities are providing businesses the head start that they need to succeed.'}{'symbol': 'MCK', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Mckesson Sets Regular Quarterly Dividend Of $0.41 Per Share', 'text': 'SETS REGULAR QUARTERLY DIVIDEND OF $0.41PER SHARE.'}{'symbol': 'MU', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Micron Technology, Inc. Introduces the Micron® X100 SSD', 'text': 'Micron Technology, Inc. announced a breakthrough in nonvolatile memory technology with the introduction of the SSD, the Micron® X100 SSD. The Micron X100 SSD is the first solution in a family of products from Micron targeting storage- and memory-intensive applications for the data center. These solutions will leverage the strengths of 3D XPoint™ technology and usher in a new tier in the memory-to-storage hierarchy with higher capacity and persistence than DRAM, along with higher endurance and performance than NAND. With a combination of high bandwidth, low latency, high quality of service (QoS) and high endurance, the Micron X100 SSD provides game-changing performance for big data applications and transactional workloads. The Micron X100 SSD accelerates data center applications by delivering larger amounts of data in real time, and it dramatically increases the speed of data transactions while maintaining predictably fast service for quicker time to insights. The Micron X100 SSD will be in limited sampling with select customers this quarter.'}{'symbol': 'MHK', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Mohawk Industries, Inc. Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter of 2019', 'text': 'Mohawk Industries, Inc. provided earnings guidance for the fourth quarter of 2019. Taking all of this into account, EPS guidance for the fourth quarter of 2019 is $2.13 to $2.23, excluding any one-time charges.'}{'symbol': 'MSI', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Motorola Solutions’ Next Generation APX NEXT Smart Radio Brings New Intelligence and Technology to Public Safety', 'text': 'Motorola Solutions announced the launch of APX NEXT™, its next-generation mission-critical Project 25 (P25) public safety radio with LTE for enhanced communications and data-centric application services. The company also announced ViQi™, a public safety virtual assistant that provides vital information to first responders in the field and allows users to operate APX NEXT via voice control. APX NEXT is the newest mission-critical P25 radio offering in Motorola Solutions’ purpose-built APX portfolio. It’s FirstNet Ready™ and comes with embedded LTE connectivity enabled by the FirstNet communications platform to quickly deliver voice and data to first responders in the field. APX NEXT is Motorola Solutions’ first APX radio to feature a touchscreen with a user interface designed specifically for public safety. The touchscreen can be used in the rain and when wearing gloves. It offers one-touch access to radio controls, large touch targets and an optimized user interface for fast navigation. ViQi voice control enables users to quickly manage radio controls through simple and intuitive voice commands. This new radio uses LMR for mission-critical voice communications and LTE broadband to power new application services including: ViQi: With ViQi Virtual Partner, first responders can retrieve information from remote databases using natural language interactions, such as ‘ViQi, run a license plate.’ SmartConnect: APX NEXT detects when an LMR signal is low and automatically switches to LTE broadband connectivity ensuring continuity of PTT voice communications. It then switches back to LMR when the signal returns with no user intervention required. SmartLocate: An officer’s location data is automatically sent over broadband to a dispatcher’s mapping console, providing dispatchers with up-to-date location information as fast as every 3 seconds. Leveraging broadband to send frequent location updates frees up your valuable LMR system resources. SmartProgramming: The radio’s software and configuration data can be rapidly updated over broadband, even when a police officer is using it. This means APX NEXT spends less time in radio shops and more time in the field.'}{'symbol': 'NDAQ', 'date': '2019-10-24 10:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Nasdaq Increases Options Market Accessibility With Nasdaq Smart Options', 'text': 'NASDAQ INCREASES OPTIONS MARKET ACCESSIBILITY WITH NASDAQ SMART OPTIONS.NASDAQ INC - LAUNCH OF NASDAQ SMART OPTIONS.NASDAQ INC - NASDAQ SMART OPTIONS A SERVICE THAT ALLOWS FOR EASIER ACCESS TO ESSENTIAL OPTIONS MARKET DATA.NASDAQ INC - NASDAQ SMART OPTIONS FEED SUPPORTS NATIONAL BEST BID AND OFFER (NBBO) AND LAST SALE TRADE MESSAGES.'}{'symbol': 'NDAQ', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Nasdaq Increases Options Market Accessibility with Nasdaq Smart Options', 'text': 'Nasdaq announced the launch of Nasdaq Smart Options, a service that allows for easier access to essential options market data. Nasdaq Smart Options provides a more manageable and less resource-intensive data feed from the U.S. options markets in real time, drawing the essential data from the standard Options Price Reporting Authority (OPRA) data feed. The Nasdaq Smart Options feed supports the National Best Bid and Offer (NBBO) and Last Sale trade messages, as well as administrative messages for all listed options. Individual exchange BBO data is excluded, which significantly reduces bandwidth cost and contributes to savings of more than 80% of the cost of connecting to the full OPRA data feed. This curated data package more closely aligns with the needs and cost parameters of the advisory community and the investing public. This means more investors can leverage options data to gain insights and make better-informed decisions.'}{'symbol': 'NDAQ', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Nasdaq Qtrly GAAP Earnings Per Share $0.90', 'text': 'QTRLY GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.90; QTRLY NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.27.QTRLY NET REVENUE $632 MILLION VERSUS $600 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.21, REVENUE VIEW $629.4 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.NASDAQ - REDUCING 2019 NON-GAAP OPERATING EXPENSE OUTLOOK TO $1.285 BILLION-$1.295 BILLION VERSUS PRIOR OUTLOOK OF $1.295 BILLION-$1.320 BILLION.RETIRING SOME ELEMENTS OF MARKETPLACE INFRASTRUCTURE, TECHNOLOGY PRODUCT OFFERINGS AS CO IMPLEMENTS NASDAQ FINANCIAL FRAMEWORK.NASDAQ - RESTRUCTURING CHARGES RELATED PRIMARILY TO NON-CASH ITEMS SUCH AS ASSET WRITE-DOWNS, ACCELERATED DEPRECIATION, THIRD-PARTY CONSULTING COSTS.AS A RESULT OF RESTRUCTURING ACTIONS, EXPECTS TO INCUR $65 MILLION-$75 MILLION IN PRE-TAX CHARGES OVER 2 YEARS (INCLUDING $30 MILLION IN Q3).NASDAQ - IMPACTS OF RESTRUCTURING PLAN WILL BE EXCLUDED FROM NON-GAAP REPORTING.'}{'symbol': 'NI', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'NiSource Inc. Appoints Deborah A. P. Hersman to Serve on the Finance Committee', 'text': 'The Board of Directors appointed Ms. Hersman to serve on the Environmental, Safety and Sustainability Committee at the time of her appointment. On October 22, 2019, the Board of Directors of NiSource Inc. appointed Ms. Deborah A. P. Hersman to serve on the Finance Committee.'}{'symbol': 'NSC', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Norfolk Southern Corporation has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $398.564 million.', 'text': 'Norfolk Southern Corporation has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $398.564 million.\n\nSecurity Name: 2.550% Senior Unsubordinated Unsecured Notes due November 1, 2029\nSecurity Type: Corporate Bond/Note (Non Convertible)\nPrincipal Amount: $400 million\nPrice\\Range: 99.641%\nDiscount Per Security: 0.65%\nSecurity Features: Callable\nCoupon Type: Fixed\n'}{'symbol': 'NTRS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Northern Trust Corporation Appoints Jennifer Gravenor as Its Austin Region President and Senior Managing Director', 'text': 'Northern Trust Corporation has announced has appointed Jennifer Gravenor as its Austin Region President and Senior Managing Director. Gravenor will be responsible for leading the firm’s team in Austin in its delivery of holistic advice, outstanding client service and growth of the wealth management business across the region. Gravenor previously served as a Senior Wealth Strategist for Northern Trust, advising affluent individuals, families, business owners, executives and charitable organizations in comprehensive wealth management, complex private banking, and trust services.'}{'symbol': 'NOC', 'date': '2019-10-24 13:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Northrop Grumman Says In Oct Received A Civil Investigative Demand From The FTC - SEC Filing', 'text': "NORTHROP GRUMMAN - IN OCTOBER, RECEIVED A CIVIL INVESTIGATIVE DEMAND FROM THE FTC - SEC FILING.NORTHROP GRUMMAN - FTC'S DEMAND REQUESTS INFORMATION ON POTENTIAL ISSUE OF COMPLIANCE WITH ORDER RELATING TO PENDING STR