ings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter and Full Year of Fiscal 2019', 'text': 'Roper Technologies, Inc. provided earnings guidance for the fourth quarter and full year of fiscal 2019. For the quarter, the company expected GAAP diluted EPS in range of $2.51 to $2.55. For the year, the company expected GAAP diluted EPS in range of $11.05 to $11.09.'}{'symbol': 'RCL', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Royal Caribbean Cruises Ltd. Unveils Bold Features on New Odyssey of the Seas', 'text': "Royal Caribbean Cruises Ltd. announced that it is setting an uncharted course for adventure with the cruise line's newest ship, Odyssey of the Seas. The first Quantum Ultra Class ship to arrive in North America will tout a brand-new look to match the fleet's most action-packed top deck to date, and a mix of record-holding hits and firsts for a game-changing cruise vacation. Odyssey's dialed-up onboard adventures, two-level pool deck designed for downtime under the sun and stars, and a collection of restaurants primed to please every palate will all be set against some of the world's most picturesque backdrops, including the vibrant islands of the Caribbean and idyllic coasts of the eastern Mediterranean."}{'symbol': 'NOW', 'date': '2019-10-24 21:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'ServiceNow Reports Q3 Adj EPS Of $1.03', 'text': 'SERVICENOW REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.SUBSCRIPTION REVENUES OF $835 MILLION IN Q3 2019, REPRESENTING 33% YEAR-OVER-YEAR GROWTH.QTRLY EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.22.QTRLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.03.QTRLY  TOTAL REVENUES $885.8 MILLION, UP 32%.SEES 2019 GAAP SUBSCRIPTION REVENUES $3,240 MILLION - $3,245 MILLION.SEES 2019 NON GAAP SUBSCRIPTION REVENUE $3,302 MILLION - $3,307 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.88, REVENUE VIEW $885.0 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $3.22, REVENUE VIEW $3.46 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QTRLY DILUTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.21.'}{'symbol': 'LUV', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Southwest Airlines Co. Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Southwest Airlines Co. Announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced total revenue was USD 5,639 million compared to USD 5,575 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 819 million compared to USD 798 million a year ago. Net income was USD 659 million compared to USD 615 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.24 compared to USD 1.08 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 1.23 compared to USD 1.08 a year ago. For the nine months, total revenue was USD 16,698 million compared to USD 16,261 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 2,292 million compared to USD 2,386 million a year ago. Net income was USD 1,787 million compared to USD 1,811 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 3.3 compared to USD 3.13 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 3.29 compared to USD 3.13 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'SWK', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Stanley Black & Decker, Inc. Revises Earnings Guidance for the Year 2019', 'text': 'Stanley Black & Decker, Inc. revised earnings guidance for the year 2019. The company management is revising its 2019 EPS outlook to $6.50 - $6.60 from $7.50 - $7.70 on a GAAP basis.'}{'symbol': 'SIVB', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Svb Financial Group Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'SVB Financial Group announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced net interest income was USD 520.644 million compared to USD 493.222 million a year ago. Net income was USD 267.281 million compared to USD 274.817 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 5.19 compared to USD 5.16 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 5.15 compared to USD 5.1 a year ago. For the nine months, net interest income was USD 1,562.933 million compared to USD 1,379.528 million a year ago. Net income was USD 874.000 million compared to USD 707.576 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 16.8 compared to USD 13.33 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 16.67 compared to USD 13.15 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'SNPS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Synopsys Introduces PrimeECO Solution for Zero-Iteration Signoff-Driven Design Closure', 'text': "Synopsys, Inc. announced the Synopsys PrimeECO design closure solution, the industry's first signoff-driven solution that achieves signoff closure with zero iterations. Signoff closure has emerged as one of the top challenges in digital design implementation, consuming up to 50% of the design schedule, mainly driven by rapidly increasing signoff scenarios and physical complexity at advanced nodes. The PrimeECO solution uniquely combines the efficiency to manage unlimited signoff scenario views with the scalability of incrementally enabled integrated physical implementation and signoff capabilities, delivering a 10X productivity boost for system-on-chip (SoC) designers by eliminating costly iterations between implementation and signoff. The PrimeECO design closure solution features an innovative machine-learning-driven Hybrid Timing View technology that addresses the increasing signoff scenarios by predicting optimal trade-offs between required compute resource and desired timing accuracy. The Hybrid Timing View deploys the PrimeTime signoff engine for real-time updates on accuracy-critical scenarios, while ensuring complete visibility on coverage-critical scenarios through efficient static views. The efficiency of Hybrid Timing View enables thousands of timing scenarios to be loaded onto a single machine, eliminating the need for a large number of compute resources typically required for signoff coverage. To further eliminate design iterations, PrimeECO is architected on the Fusion Design Platform, the world's first artificial intelligence (AI) enhanced, cloud-ready design platform with direct access to incrementally enabled placement, routing, extraction, physical verification, and signoff technologies from Synopsys' market-leading portfolio of solutions, including IC Compiler II place-and route, Fusion Compiler RTL-to-GDSII, IC Validator physical verification, StarRC extraction, PrimeTime, PrimePower, and PrimeYield. Within this single-environment design closure cockpit, not only is every change fully implemented and validated, but it also creates new opportunities for placement, routing, and timing co-optimization to achieve power, performance, and area (PPA) results previously impossible in traditional design closure flows. The exclusive PrimeECO solution is available to all designers innovating on the Fusion Design Platform, as well as industry-standard DEF databases. The intuitive cockpit also provides a unique graphical user interface to overlay Hybrid Timing View on design visualization for final touch-ups, including an open database interface available to custom scripts for user-driven optimization."}{'symbol': 'TMUS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'At&T, Sprint, T-Mobile And Verizon To Form Joint Venture', 'text': 'Oct 24  - AT&T Inc <T.N>::AT&T, SPRINT, T-MOBILE AND VERIZON FORM JOINT VENTURE TO TRANSFORM MESSAGING EXPERIENCE.SPRINT -  CCMI JV IS WORKING TO DEVELOP AND DEPLOY STANDARDS-BASED, INTEROPERABLE MESSAGING SERVICE STARTING WITH ANDROID AND EXPECTED IN 2020.'}{'symbol': 'TROW', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'T. Rowe Price Group Inc Quarterly Non-GAAP Diluted Earnings Per Common Share Of $2.13', 'text': 'T. ROWE PRICE GROUP REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.T. ROWE PRICE GROUP INC QUARTERLY  EARNINGS PER COMMON SHARE OF $2.23.T. ROWE PRICE GROUP INC QUARTERLY  NON-GAAP DILUTED EARNINGS PER COMMON SHARE OF $2.13.T. ROWE PRICE GROUP INC QUARTERLY NET REVENUES OF $1.43 BILLION VERSUS $1.4 BILLION.T. ROWE PRICE GROUP INC SAYS ASSETS UNDER MANAGEMENT END QUARTER AT $1.126 TRILLION.T. ROWE PRICE GROUP INC - NET CLIENT INFLOWS OF $2.5 BILLION IN QUARTER.T. ROWE PRICE GROUP INC QTRLY INVESTMENT ADVISORY FEES $1,303.4 MILLION VERSUS $1,263.3 MILLION.'}{'symbol': 'TROW', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'T Rowe Price Hires Tim Coyne to Lead its Newly Established ETF Team', 'text': "T Rowe Price have launched their own ETF businesses and each hired a specialist from a rival group to head up their respective operations. T Rowe Price hired State Street veteran Tim Coyne to lead its newly established ETF team. At T. Rowe Price, Coyne joined the firm after having served over 13 years at State Street Global Advisors. His most recent role was senior managing director and global head of capital markets within its SPDR ETF unit. Prior to that, he spent four years as the firm's managing director of ETF institutional sales and global capital markets. Coyne has also held positions at the New York Stock Exchange, where he was managing director of ETF sales and marketing."}{'symbol': 'TMO', 'date': '2019-10-24 08:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Thermo Fisher Scientific Reports Third Quarter 2019 Results', 'text': 'THERMO FISHER SCIENTIFIC REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $2.94.Q3 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.88.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $2.87 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.Q3 REVENUE INCREASED 6% TO $6.27 BILLION.RAISING ITS 2019 REVENUE AND EARNINGS GUIDANCE.RAISING 2019 REVENUE GUIDANCE TO A NEW RANGE OF $25.34 TO $25.50 BILLION.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $6.18 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.RAISING 2019 ADJUSTED EPS GUIDANCE TO $12.28 TO $12.34, VERSUS PREVIOUS GUIDANCE OF $12.16 TO $12.26.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $12.25, REVENUE VIEW $25.43 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.'}{'symbol': 'TSCO', 'date': '2019-10-24 11:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Tractor Supply Co Reports Q3 Earnings Per Share $1.02', 'text': 'MPANY REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 FINANCIAL RESULTS.Q3 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.04.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.02.Q3 SAME STORE SALES ROSE 2.9 PERCENT.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $1.03 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FY 2019 ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.68 TO $4.72 EXCLUDING ITEMS.SEES FY 2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE $4.66 TO $4.70.SEES FY 2019 SALES $8.4 BILLION TO $8.42 BILLION.Q3 SALES $1.98 BILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $2 BILLION.FY2019 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $4.73, REVENUE VIEW $8.44 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.FOR FISCAL 2019, COMPANY CONTINUES TO FORECAST CAPITAL EXPENDITURES IN RANGE OF $225 MILLION TO $250 MILLION.SEES 2019 COMPARABLE STORE SALES GROWTH OF 3.2% TO 3.4%.'}{'symbol': 'TSCO', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Tractor Supply Company Revises Earnings Guidance for the Year 2019', 'text': 'Tractor Supply Company revised earnings guidance for the year 2019. Based on year-to-date performance, the company is providing the following updated guidance for the expected results of operations in fiscal 2019: net sales of $8.40 billion to $8.42 billion, compared to its previous expectation of $8.40 billion to $8.46 billion; net income of $564 million to $569 million, compared to its previous guidance of $562 million to $575 million; and earnings per diluted share of $4.66 to $4.70, compared to its previous guidance of $4.65 to $4.75.'}{'symbol': 'TWTR', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Twitter Inc Reports GAAP Earnings Of $0.05 Per Share', 'text': 'QUARTERLY GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.05.QUARTERLY NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.17.QUARTERLY TOTAL REVENUE $824 MILLION, UP 9%.QUARTERLY ADJUSTED EARNINGS PER SHARE, EXCLUDING NET BENEFIT FROM DEFERRED TAX ASSETS WAS $0.05.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $0.20, REVENUE VIEW $874.0 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.QUARTERLY ADVERTISING REVENUE $702 MILLION, UP 8%.QUARTERLY AVERAGE MONETIZABLE DAILY ACTIVE USERS 145 MILLION VERSUS 124 MILLION.QUARTERLY AVERAGE U.S. MDAU 30 MILLION VERSUS 26 MILLION.QUARTERLY AVERAGE INTERNATIONAL MDAU 115 MILLION VERSUS 98 MILLION.ENDED THE QUARTER WITH ABOUT $5.8 BILLION IN CASH, CASH EQUIVALENTS AND MARKETABLE SECURITIES.SEES Q4 REVENUE OF $940 MILLION-$1.01 BILLION; SEES Q4 GAAP OPERATING. INCOME $130 MILLION-$170 MILLION.Q4 REVENUE VIEW $1.06 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES 2019 CAPITAL EXPENDITURE TO BE AT OR NEAR LOW END OF PREVIOUS OUTLOOK OF $550 MILLION-$600 MILLION.Q3 REVENUE GROWTH REFLECTS STRENGTH IN SEPT. IN U.S., NUMBER OF HEADWINDS INCL. REVENUE PRODUCT ISSUES, GREATER-THAN-EXPECTED AD SEASONALITY IN JULY & AUG.SAYS JAPAN REMAINS SECOND LARGEST MARKET, CONTRIBUTING $129 MILLION, OR 16% OF TOTAL Q3 REVENUE.IN Q3, DISCOVERED AND TOOK STEPS TO REMEDIATE, BUGS THAT PRIMARILY AFFECTED LEGACY MAP PRODUCT.IN Q3, ALSO DISCOVERED CERTAIN PERSONALIZATION AND DATA SETTINGS WERE NOT OPERATING AS EXPECTED.BELIEVE IN AGGREGATE, BUGS AND SETTINGS ISSUES REDUCED REVENUE GROWTH BY 3 OR MORE POINTS IN Q3.'}{'symbol': 'TWTR', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Twitter, Inc. Provides Earnings Guidance for the Fourth Quarter of 2019', 'text': 'Twitter, Inc. provides earnings guidance for the fourth quarter of 2019. For the quarter, the company expects total\xa0revenue to be between $940 million and $1.01 billion and operating income to be between $130 million and $170 million.'}{'symbol': 'UHS', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Universal Health Services, Inc. Revises Earnings Guidance for the Full Year Ending December 31, 2019', 'text': 'Universal Health Services, Inc. revised earnings guidance for the full year ending December 31, 2019. Based upon the operating trends and financial results experienced during the first nine months of 2019, the company is revising its estimated range of adjusted net in come attributable to UHS for the year ended December 31, 2019 to $9.60 to $9.90 per diluted share as compared to the previously provided range of $9.70 to $10.40 per diluted share. This revised estimated guidance range decreases the lower end of the previously provided range 1.0% and decreases the upper end of the previously provided range by 4.8%. Contributing to, and included in, the revised estimated earnings guidance range for the year ended December 31, 2019 is the above-mentioned unrealized loss of $0.11 per diluted share ($12.5 million pre-tax), recorded during the first nine months of 2019 resulting from a decrease in the market value of shares of certain marketable securities held for investment and classified as available for sale.'}{'symbol': 'VLO', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Valero Energy Posts Qtrly Revenue of $27,249 Million', 'text': 'VALERO ENERGY REPORTS THIRD QUARTER 2019 RESULTS.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE $1.48.QTRLY REFINERY THROUGHPUT CAPACITY UTILIZATION WAS 94 PERCENT.Q4 MARKET CONDITIONS LOOK FAVORABLE WITH IMPROVED GASOLINE AND DISTILLATE CRACKS.THROUGHPUT VOLUMES AVERAGED 2.95 MILLION BARRELS PER DAY IN Q3 OF 2019.QTRLY REVENUE $27,249 MILLION VERSUS $30,849 MILLION.Q3 EARNINGS PER SHARE VIEW $1.35, REVENUE VIEW $24.21 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.CONTINUES TO EXPECT TO INVEST APPROXIMATELY $2.5 BILLION OF CAPITAL IN BOTH 2019 AND 2020.VALERO ENERGY - EXPECT TO SEE CONTINUED PRODUCT STRENGTH WITH INVENTORIES AT LOWER LEVELS AND SOUR CRUDE WEAKNESS.'}{'symbol': 'VLO', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Valero Energy Corporation Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'Valero Energy Corporation announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 27,249 million compared to USD 30,849 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 881 million compared to USD 1,219 million a year ago. Net income was USD 609 million compared to USD 856 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.48 compared to USD 2.01 a year ago. For the nine months, sales was USD 80,445 million compared to USD 88,303 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 2,097 million compared to USD 3,273 million a year ago. Net income was USD 1,362 million compared to USD 2,170 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 3.28 compared to USD 5.05 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'VRSN', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Verisign, Inc. Reports Earnings Results for the Third Quarter Ended September 30, 2019', 'text': 'VeriSign, Inc. announced earnings results for the third quarter ended September 30, 2019. For the third quarter, the company announced sales was USD 308.421 million compared to USD 305.777 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 205.616 million compared to USD 194.997 million a year ago. Net income was USD 153.913 million compared to USD 137.680 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 1.3 compared to USD 1.13 a year ago. For the nine months, sales was USD 921.118 million compared to USD 907.517 million a year ago. Operating income was USD 607.561 million compared to USD 573.426 million a year ago. Net income was USD 463.974 million compared to USD 400.294 million a year ago. Basic earnings per share was USD 3.9 compared to USD 3.6 a year ago. Diluted earnings per share was USD 3.89 compared to USD 3.25 a year ago.'}{'symbol': 'VRSK', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'LV= General Insurance Signs Three-year Renewal to Use Verisk Claim Solutions to Enhance UK Property Claim Operations', 'text': 'Verisk announced that leading UK insurer LV= General Insurance has renewed its use of the Xactimate® claims estimation tool and the real-time claims management solution XactAnalysis® to support its property claims for a further three years. As part of this ongoing strategic relationship, Verisk and LV= GI have closely collaborated on several major projects to develop and deliver highly effective capabilities, including a purpose-built Building Contractor Network to enable LV= GI to manage its growing network of suppliers. Under the Building Contractor Network initiative, Verisk provides LV= GI with advanced supply chain management and performance monitoring for a nationwide network of building suppliers, including a customised Schedule of Rates to ensure policyholders receive the high level of service. Verisk played an integral role in onboarding specialist suppliers into the Building Contractor Network, providing training and support to establish supplier best practices. The Building Contractor Network delivers estimation and settlement transparency, configurable supplier management, and performance monitoring, which ultimately helps shorten claim life cycles.'}{'symbol': 'VRTX', 'date': '2019-10-24 09:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Vertex Announces Agreement With Nhs England For Access To All Licensed Cystic Fibrosis Medicines', 'text': 'VERTEX ANNOUNCES AGREEMENT WITH NHS ENGLAND FOR ACCESS TO ALL LICENSED CYSTIC FIBROSIS MEDICINES.VERTEX PHARMACEUTICALS - IN ADDITION TO ENGLAND, REIMBURSEMENT AGREEMENTS HAVE ALSO RECENTLY BEEN ANNOUNCED IN SCOTLAND, AUSTRALIA AND SPAIN..VERTEX PHARMACEUTICALS - ELIGIBLE PATIENTS IN ENGLAND WILL HAVE ACCESS TO ORKAMBIAND SYMKEVI EXPANDED ACCESS TO KALYDECO(® )(IVACAFTOR).'}{'symbol': 'VRTX', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated Announces Agreement with NHS England for Access to All Licensed Cystic Fibrosis Medicines', 'text': 'Vertex Pharmaceuticals Incorporated announced an access agreement with NHS England for all currently licensed Vertex cystic fibrosis (CF) medicines and any future indications of these medicines. This means that within 30 days patients with CF in England ages 2 years and older who have two copies of the F508del mutation in the cystic fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator(CFTR) gene can be prescribed ORKAMBI® (lumacaftor/ivacaftor) by their doctor and CF patients ages 12 years and older who either have two copies of the F508del mutation or one copy of the F508del mutation and a copy of one of the other 14 licensed mutations can be prescribed SYMKEVI® (tezacaftor/ivacaftor) in combination with ivacaftor. The agreement also offers expanded access to KALYDECO® (ivacaftor) to include people ages 18 years and older who have the R117H mutation and those patients ages 12 months and older who have one of the nine licensed gating mutations.'}{'symbol': 'V', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Visa Inc. Declares Quarterly Cash Dividend, Payable on December 3, 2019', 'text': 'On October 22, 2019, the board of directors of Visa Inc. declared a quarterly cash dividend in the aggregate amount of $0.30 per share of class A common stock (determined in the case of class B and C common stock and series B and C convertible participating preferred stock on an as-converted basis), payable on December 3, 2019, to all holders of record as of November 15, 2019.'}{'symbol': 'VMC', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Vulcan Materials Company Presents at Stephens Nashville Investment Conference, Nov-13-2019 02:30 PM', 'text': 'Vulcan Materials Company Presents at Stephens Nashville Investment Conference, Nov-13-2019 02:30 PM. Venue: Omni Nashville Hotel, 250 Fifth Avenue S, Nashville, Tennessee, United States. Speakers: Mark D. Warren, Vice President of Investor Relations.'}{'symbol': 'WFC', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Wells Fargo & Company has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $3.5 billion.', 'text': 'Wells Fargo & Company has completed a Fixed-Income Offering in the amount of $3.5 billion.\n\nSecurity Name: Fixed to Floating Rate Senior Notes due October 30, 2030\nSecurity Type: Corporate Bond/Note (Non Convertible)\nPrincipal Amount: $3.5 billion\nPrice\\Range: 100%\nDiscount Per Security: 0.45%\nSecurity Features: Callable; MTN; Variable Rate\nCoupon Type: Variable\n'}{'symbol': 'WST', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'West Pharmaceutical Services, Inc. Raises Earnings Guidance for the Full Year 2019', 'text': 'West Pharmaceutical Services, Inc. raised earnings guidance for the full year 2019. The company is raising its full-year 2019 net sales guidance to a new range of between $1.815 billion and $1.825 billion, compared to the prior guidance range of between $1.810 billion and $1.825 billion. Organic sales growth is expected to be approximately 8%. Net sales guidance includes a headwind of $54 million for the full-year 2019 based on current foreign exchange rates, compared to prior guidance of a full-year negative impact of $42 million.'}{'symbol': 'WDC', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Western Digital Corp. Introduces Next-Level Storage Solutions for NAS Environments', 'text': "Western Digital Corp. introduced an array of purpose-built storage solutions for small businesses and home offices leveraging NAS environments. The solutions include the first-ever WD Red® SSDs, which enhance performance and caching abilities in a hybrid NAS environment, as well as a 14TB capacity for the WD Red and WD Red Pro HDDs. SSD Performance to Support High-Speed Connectivity: With the increase in virtualization, 10GbE (10 Gigabit Ethernet) and higher connectivity speeds are becoming an essential feature set in modern NAS systems. To help minimize a performance bottleneck, SSD speeds are crucial. To fully support the requirements of these environments, storage device durability, speed and capacity remain heavily in demand. Building on the proven reliability of Western Digital’s WD Red product portfolio, the solutions are built to transform pain points to profits for the end user. When utilized as a caching solution in a NAS system, the WD Red SA500 SSD helps to boost performance while the new higher capacity WD Red and WD Red Pro HDDs offer more storage space in the same NAS device. Product Details: New products introduced are: WD Red SA500 NAS SATA SSD: Purpose-built for NAS enthusiasts, the latest WD Red SA500 NAS SATA SSD offers capacities from 500GB up to 4TB1 (2.5-inch only) and creates an environment optimized for 10GbE networks as well as caching in NAS systems to rapidly access frequently used files. With superior endurance for heavy read and write loads demanded by NAS in a 24/7 environment, the drive supports OLTP databases, multi-user environments, photo rendering, 4K and 8K video editing. WD Red NAS Hard Drive: Complementary to the WD Red SA500 NAS SATA SSD, the latest WD Red HDD capacity increase to 14TB1 is designed for use in NAS systems with up to 8 bays. Ideal for small-and-home-office 24/7 environments, the drive supports up to a 180 TB/year workload rate. WD Red Pro NAS Hard Drive: Built like the WD Red HDD with a boost for professional NAS workloads and up to 14TB1 capacity, the WD Red Pro HDD supports up to 24 bays. With 3D Active Balance Plus technology and error recovery controls with NASware™ 3.0 technology, the drive operates with enhanced reliability. Pricing and Availability: The WD Red SA500 SSD comes in capacities of 500GB up to 2TB for the M.2 form factor and ranges in price from $72.00 up to $297.00 (MSRP USD) in the U.S. The 2.5-inch form factor of the WD Red SA500 SSD comes in capacities of 500GB up to 4TB and ranges in price from $75.00 to $600.00 (MSRP USD) in the U.S. Both form factors of WD Red SA500 SSDs are currently available in limited quantities at the WD store in the U.S. and will be available globally in November at select Western Digital retailers, e-tailers, resellers, and system integrators. The WD Red NAS HDD in 14TB capacity is priced at $450.00 (MSRP USD) in the U.S. and the WD Red NAS Pro HDD in 14TB capacity is priced at $525.00 (MSRP USD) in the U.S. These 14TB HDD products will be available globally in November at select Western Digital retailers, e-tailers, resellers, system integrators and at the WD store. The new WD Red products join Western Digital’s portfolio of HDD and SSD solutions that are purpose-built for a range of applications in enterprise, client and gaming markets. For enterprise customers, Western Digital recently enhanced its WD Gold Enterprise Class HDD storage solution, now available in capacities up to 14TB1. Enabling the possibilities of data, Western Digital offers one of the industry's broadest portfolio of products and solutions to help people capture, preserve, access and transform their content."}{'symbol': 'WU', 'date': '2019-10-24 07:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Western Union Expands Its Global Platform Now To New Partners In Asia', 'text': "WESTERN UNION EXPANDS ITS GLOBAL PLATFORM NOW TO NEW PARTNERS IN ASIA.JAPAN'S KYODAI REMITTANCE AND KOREA'S FINTECH HANPASS MONEY TRANSFER COMPANIES WILL NOW USE WESTERN UNION'S GLOBAL NETWORK."}{'symbol': 'WHR', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'KinderCare Education and Whirlpool Open New Onsite Childcare Center', 'text': 'Whirlpool has partnered with KinderCare Education to open The Eddy, its first onsite childcare center. The center features an indoor terrarium in the lobby, an indoor multipurpose room, outdoor playgrounds with a soccer field, a whimsical playhouse, tricycle paths, a tree house, and an outdoor stage for plays and moments of make-believe. And because the center is onsite, Whirlpool employees can visit their children anytime, drop into classes, join special outings and events, and even nurse.'}{'symbol': 'XEL', 'date': '2019-10-24 22:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Xcel Energy Inc. Revises Earnings Guidance for the Full Year 2019; Provides Earnings Guidance for the Year 2020', 'text': 'Xcel Energy Inc. revised earnings guidance for the full year 2019 and provided earnings guidance for the year 2020. The company expected earnings to the upper half of 2019 guidance range. the company narrows its 2019 EPS guidance range to $2.60 to $2.65 from $2.55 to $2.65.The company have issued 2020 earnings guidance of $2.73 to $2.83 per share, which is consistent with 5-7% growth objective.'}{'symbol': 'XLNX', 'date': '2019-10-24 18:30:00-04:56', 'title': 'Xilinx Reports Fiscal Second Quarter 2020 Results', 'text': 'XILINX REPORTS FISCAL SECOND QUARTER 2020 RESULTS.Q2 NON-GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.94.Q2 GAAP EARNINGS PER SHARE $0.89.Q2 REVENUE $833 MILLION VERSUS REFINITIV IBES ESTIMATE OF $824.8 MILLION.Q2 EARNINGS PER SHARE ESTIMATE $0.89 -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.BOARD OF DIRECTORS APPROVES SHARE REPURCHASE AUTHORIZATION OF UP TO $1.0 BILLION.COMPANY NOW EXPECTS FULL YEAR REVENUE GROWTH OF APPROXIMATELY 6%.XILINX - SEES Q3 REVENUES $710 MILLION- $740 MILLION.SEES FISCAL YEAR 2020 GAAP REVENUES $3,210 MILLION-$3,280 MILLION.Q3 REVENUE VIEW $844.9 MILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.SEES FISCAL YEAR 2020 GAAP GROSS MARGIN BETWEEN 65.5% - 67.5%.FY2020 REVENUE VIEW $3.40 BILLION -- REFINITIV IBES DATA.XILINX - Q3 AND 2020 GUIDANCE TAKES INTO ACCOUNT IMPACT FROM U.S. GOVERNMENT\'S ANNOUNCED EXPORT RESTRICTION TO ONE OF OUR CUSTOMERS IN CHINA."FIRST HALF OF OUR CURRENT FISCAL YEAR REMAINED STRONG DESPITE IMPACT OF CONTINUED BUSINESS RESTRICTIONS RELATED TO HUAWEI".FOR FISCAL 2020, WE BELIEVE THAT Q3 WILL BE OUR LOW POINT.EXPECT TO SEE A RETURN TO SEQUENTIAL REVENUE GROWTH IN OUR Q4.'}